window.GEAR_BOOK_CONTENTS["book-30"] = [{"id":1,"rawContent":"# 第一章：死者比活人更有禮貌\n\n濱江市的十一月，江霧濃得像是一鍋煮沸後放涼的隔夜濃湯。\n\n清晨五點四十分，老船埠的廢棄浮橋邊漂上來一具屍體，卡在兩根長滿墨綠色青苔的防撞木樁之間，隨著渾濁的江水微微起伏。\n\n當市公安局刑偵支隊副隊長周成林裹著他那件洗得發白的軍綠色夾克、手裡捧著直徑十公分的巨型不鏽鋼保溫杯趕到現場時，警戒線外已經圍了三層早起晨跑和大清早買菜的市民。\n\n「散了散了，各位大爺大嬸，這不是劇組在拍電影，沒發雞蛋也沒發便當。」老周吸溜了一口滾燙的枸杞黨參茶，嗓音沙啞得像兩塊砂紙在摩擦，「退到黃線外面去，踩壞了現場腳印，等會兒局裡的罰單可直接寄到你們家信箱。」\n\n警戒線被拉開一條縫，一道高挑瘦削的身影無聲無息地鑽了進來。\n\n那人穿著一件熨燙得稜角分明的深灰色羊毛風衣，裡面是雪白挺括的立領襯衫，鼻樑上架著一副極細的純銀半框眼鏡。他手裡提著一隻沉重的黑色鋁合金法醫勘驗箱，走路時皮鞋落在潮濕的碎石灘上，節奏精準得像是一台剛校準過的石英鐘。\n\n「小裴，來啦？」老周轉過頭，臉上堆起彌勒佛般的市井笑容，「瞧瞧，剛打撈上來的熱乎……呃，不對，江水拔涼，估計早凍透了。」\n\n裴以安停下腳步，修長的手指輕輕推了一下眼鏡架，目光甚至沒有在老周那張堆滿褶子的笑臉上停留半秒。\n\n「周副隊長，根據熱力學定律與人體死後生物物理變化，在攝氏七度的流水環境中，不存在任何『熱乎』的可能。」裴以安的聲音清冷平淡，乾淨得不帶一絲煙火氣，「另外，您保溫杯裡散發出來的熟地黃與當歸氣味，已經嚴重干擾了現場半徑三米內的揮發性化學物質採樣。」\n\n老周嘿嘿一笑，絲毫不惱，反而慢悠悠地擰緊了杯蓋：「行行行，我這不是怕你大清早低血糖嘛。昨晚市局地下的解剖室又亮了一宿，你小子是打算把自己也醃成標本？」\n\n「死者比活人更有禮貌。」裴以安從風衣口袋裡摸出一隻扁平的馬口鐵盒，修長的手指優雅地彈開盒蓋，取出一顆深綠色的高濃度薄荷糖扔進嘴裡，「至少，他們躺在那裡的時候，既不會撒謊，也不會強迫別人喝充滿草本腐敗氣味的植物浸泡液。」\n\n老周被噎得乾咳了一聲，旁邊提著物證箱小跑過來的實習法醫助理蘇棠忍不住噗嗤笑出了聲。\n\n「裴老師早！周隊早！」蘇棠一邊喘著氣一邊遞上無菌手套和鞋套，「現場初步溫度測量完成，水溫6.8度，環境氣溫8.2度。」\n\n裴以安戴上乳膠手套，那雙手骨節分明，穩得沒有半分顫抖。他半跪在潮濕冰冷的防水油布旁，目光落在剛被抬上岸的死者身上。\n\n死者是一名男性，目測年齡在三十歲上下，穿著一身剪裁考驗的名貴訂製西裝，但此刻昂貴的羊絨布料已被江水浸泡得沉重變形，領口歪斜，腳上只剩下一隻手工縫線的牛津皮鞋。\n\n「體表無劇烈打鬥造成的防禦性傷痕，指甲縫隙乾淨，沒有泥沙殘留。」裴以安的指尖輕輕劃過死者的下頜與頸部，「顏面部發紺不明顯，眼結合膜下未見典型的機械性窒息出血點。老周，這不是失足溺水。」\n\n老周臉上的玩世不恭瞬間收斂乾淨，眼底閃過一抹老刑警特有的獵犬般的光芒：「不是淹死的？可他是從江心漩渦一路沖到浮橋這兒的。」\n\n「溺水者的呼吸道與肺部會吸入大量江水與浮游生物，導致肺氣腫並在口鼻周圍形成微細白色蕈狀泡沫。」裴以安解開死者那件價值不菲的真絲領帶，動作溫柔得像在對待一件易碎的瓷器，「他的口鼻乾淨得像是剛在五星級飯店的鵝絨枕頭上睡了一覺。他是死後才被拋入江中的。」\n\n「謀殺拋屍。」老周沉著嗓子吐出四個字，抬頭看了一眼灰濛濛的江面。\n\n「精確地說，是一場偽裝極其拙劣、但在時間點上極其傲慢的謀殺。」裴以安站起身，摘下第一層手套，神情嚴肅得近乎冷酷，「死者胃部有明顯的異常膨隆。現場條件不具備深入檢查資格，立刻封存遺體，送回局裡一號解剖室。」\n\n四十分鐘後，市公安局地下一層。\n\n這裡是整座大樓最安靜的角落。空氣中瀰漫著高濃度消毒水、低溫冷氣與福馬林混合的特有冷冽氣味。\n\n無影燈灑下刺目的白光，將不銹鋼解剖台照耀得如同一座聖潔而冰冷的祭壇。\n\n裴以安換上了全套無菌手術服，淡藍色的防護面罩後，那雙清澈的眼眸專注得沒有一絲雜質。老周靠在解剖室門口的觀察窗旁，手裡的保溫杯換成了一根沒點燃的香菸，習慣性地放在鼻子底下嗅著。\n\n「解剖記錄，案號1107，無名男性浮屍。」蘇棠坐在記錄台前，手指飛快地敲擊著鍵盤。\n\n裴以安握住四號解剖刀，刀鋒在死者的胸骨上方輕輕一懸，低聲道了一句：「打擾了。」\n\n這是他每次動刀前唯一的儀式，聲音極輕，宛如一聲不經意的嘆息。\n\n冰冷鋒利的手術刀順著頸部正中線一路滑下，切開胸骨、腹壁，組織在熟練無比的手法下宛如花瓣般向兩側翻開。\n\n「胸腔未見積液，雙肺表面蒼白、萎陷，證實死前未曾發生自主性劇烈嗆水。」裴以安的動作極快，解剖剪在指間靈活旋轉，「切開腹腔，注意氣味採樣。」\n\n蘇棠立刻端起採樣針筒湊上前去。當胃壁被劃開一道三公分的小口時，一股奇異的氣味悄然瀰漫開來。\n\n那不是尋常腐敗或胃酸的刺鼻酸臭，而是一種混合了苦杏仁、乾枯玫瑰花瓣與高純度蜂蠟的詭異甜香。\n\n「這是什麼味道？」站在防護玻璃外的老周忍不住直起腰，把香菸從嘴邊拿開，「死者生前喝了香水？」\n\n「不是香水。」裴以安的眉頭第一次微微蹙起，他拿起一把純銀解剖鑷，緩緩探入死者胃壁幽門前端。\n\n鑷子頂端碰到了一個堅硬的物體，發出一聲極其微弱但清脆的金屬碰撞聲——「錚」。\n\n解剖室裡的所有人在那一瞬間屏住了呼吸。\n\n裴以安手腕極穩，鑷子一點一點向外抽拉。隨著黏液被生理鹽水沖洗乾淨，包裹在一層半透明淡黃色外科骨蠟中的神秘物體，終於暴露在刺目的無影燈下。\n\n那不是毒丸，也不是走私鑽石。\n\n那是一枚長約六公分、造型古樸華麗的純黃銅古典鑰匙。\n\n鑰匙的握柄被精細地雕刻成一隻展翅的銜尾蛇圖騰，蛇眼鑲嵌著兩顆極小的暗紅色石榴石，在冰冷的燈光下閃爍著森然的微光。而在鑰匙的骨幹側面，赫然用微雕技術刻著一行工整的拉丁文縮寫與一個神秘的四位數字：\n\n**「M.S. 1934」**\n\n「我的老天爺……」蘇棠倒吸了一口涼氣，手中的記錄筆差點掉在地上，「誰會把一把古董鑰匙吞進肚子裡？」\n\n「不是吞進去的。」裴以安用鑷子夾起那枚沉甸甸的鑰匙，眼神前所未有地凌厲，「死者的食道黏膜有逆向挫傷出血，賁門括約肌撕裂。這把鑰匙，是在他瀕死神志不清時，被人用管飼器具強行塞進胃袋深處的。」\n\n觀察窗外的老周猛地一拳砸在窗框上，保溫杯裡的水花晃了出來。\n\n「他不是在自保，兇手也不是在藏匿贓物。」裴以安喃喃自語，鏡片後倒映著那隻銜尾蛇的冷光，「兇手是把這個人當成了一隻裝滿謎題的活體保險箱，然後把打開真相的鑰匙，藏在了死者的屍體深處。」\n\n解剖室的鐘聲在這一刻敲響了整點，沉悶悠長的迴音在地下一層久久迴盪。\n\n裴以安轉過身，隔著玻璃看向神色凝重的老周，薄唇輕啟：\n\n「老周，叫外勤備車吧。死者已經把信交給我們了，現在該輪到我們去找那扇三十年前被鎖上的門了。」","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 1: The Dead Are More Polite Than the Living\n\nIn November, the river mist over Binjiang City was as thick as an overnight pot of rich soup that had boiled and then cooled.\n\nAt 5:40 a.m., a corpse floated up near the abandoned pontoon bridge of the old docks, wedged between two collision pilings overgrown with dark green moss, bobbing gently with the turbid river currents.\n\nWhen Zhou Chenglin, Deputy Captain of the Municipal Criminal Investigation Detachment, arrived wrapped in his washed-out army-green jacket and clutching a giant stainless-steel thermos ten centimeters in diameter, three rings of morning joggers and early-market grocery shoppers had already swarmed outside the police cordon.\n\n\"All right, disperse, aunts and uncles! This isn't a movie set—no free eggs or boxed lunches here,\" Old Zhou slurped a mouthful of boiling goji and codonopsis tea, his voice rasping like two sheets of sandpaper rubbing together. \"Step back beyond the yellow tape! Trample the footprints on this scene, and the bureau's fines will be mailed straight to your mailboxes.\"\n\nThe cordon was lifted a sliver, and a tall, slender figure slipped quietly inside.\n\nThe newcomer wore an immaculately pressed charcoal-grey wool trench coat over a crisp, white stand-collar shirt, with ultra-thin silver half-rim spectacles resting on the bridge of his nose. He carried a heavy black aluminum alloy forensic kit, his leather shoes treading across the wet gravel with a precise cadence, like a freshly calibrated quartz clock.\n\n\"Little Pei, you're here?\" Old Zhou turned, his face wrinkling into a street-smart Maitreya smile. \"Take a look—freshly fished out, still warm... er, well, never mind, the river's freezing; he's probably chilled to the bone.\"\n\nPei Yi'an stopped, his slender fingers lightly nudging his glasses frame, his gaze not lingering for even half a second on Old Zhou's wrinkled grin.\n\n\"Deputy Captain Zhou, according to the laws of thermodynamics and postmortem biophysical changes in a flowing aquatic environment of seven degrees Celsius, there is zero probability of anything being 'warm,'\" Pei Yi'an's voice was crisp, calm, and utterly devoid of worldly warmth. \"Furthermore, the odor of rehmannia root and angelica wafting from your thermos has severely contaminated the sampling of volatile organic compounds within a three-meter radius.\"\n\nOld Zhou chuckled, entirely unoffended, and leisurely screwed the lid back onto his thermos. \"Alright, alright. I was just worried you'd get hypoglycemia this early. The basement autopsy lab was lit all night again—are you planning to pickle yourself into a specimen too, kid?\"\n\n\"The dead are more polite than the living,\" Pei Yi'an produced a flat tin box from his trench coat pocket. With a graceful flick of his slender fingers, the lid popped open, and he tossed a dark-green, extra-strong peppermint lozenge into his mouth. \"At the very least, while lying there, they neither tell lies nor force others to ingest plant decoctions that reek of herbal decay.\"\n\nOld Zhou gave a dry cough, completely tongue-tied, while Su Tang, the intern forensic assistant jogging over with an evidence crate, couldn't suppress a giggle.\n\n\"Morning, Teacher Pei! Morning, Captain Zhou!\" Su Tang panted as she handed over sterile gloves and shoe covers. \"Initial on-scene temperature measurements complete: water temperature 6.8°C, ambient air temperature 8.2°C.\"\n\nPei Yi'an pulled on the latex gloves. His hands were long-fingered and lean, steady without the slightest tremor. He knelt on the wet, cold waterproof tarp, his gaze falling upon the victim who had just been hauled ashore.\n\nThe deceased was male, visually estimated to be in his early thirties, dressed in an impeccably tailored bespoke designer suit. Now, however, the expensive cashmere fabric was waterlogged, heavy, and warped, the collar askew, and only a single hand-stitched Oxford shoe remained on his feet.\n\n\"No defensive wounds indicative of a violent struggle on the body; nail beds are clean, with no mud or sand trapped underneath,\" Pei Yi'an's fingertips brushed gently across the deceased's jawline and neck. \"Facial cyanosis is indistinct, and no classic mechanical asphyxiation petechial hemorrhages are visible beneath the conjunctiva. Old Zhou, this was no accidental drowning.\"\n\nThe cynical playfulness on Old Zhou's face evaporated instantly, replaced by the sharp, hound-like glint characteristic of a seasoned detective. \"Not drowned? But he was washed all the way from the mid-river vortex to the pontoon bridge here.\"\n\n\"A drowning victim's respiratory tract and lungs inhale massive quantities of river water and plankton, leading to acute pulmonary emphysema and forming fine, white mushroom-like foam around the mouth and nostrils,\" Pei Yi'an loosened the deceased's costly silk necktie, his motions tender, as if handling fragile porcelain. \"His mouth and nose are as clean as if he had just slept on a five-star hotel's goose-down pillow. He was tossed into the river post-mortem.\"\n\n\"Murder and body dump,\" Old Zhou growled four heavy words, glancing up at the murky expanse of the river.\n\n\"To be precise, a murder disguised with extreme clumsiness, yet staged with immense arrogance regarding timing,\" Pei Yi'an stood, stripping off his outer layer of gloves, his expression stern to the point of ruthlessness. \"There is pronounced, abnormal distension in the victim's epigastric region. On-scene conditions do not permit an invasive examination. Seal the remains immediately and transfer them to Autopsy Suite One at headquarters.\"\n\nForty minutes later, in Basement Level 1 of the Municipal Police Bureau.\n\nThis was the quietest sanctuary in the entire building. The air was permeated with a clinical chill—a distinctive scent mingling high-grade disinfectant, sub-zero air conditioning, and formalin.\n\nThe shadowless surgical lamps cast glaring white beams, illuminating the stainless-steel autopsy table like a sacred, frigid altar.\n\nPei Yi'an had changed into full sterile surgical scrubs; behind his pale blue protective visor, his clear eyes were focused without a speck of impurity. Old Zhou leaned against the observation window by the autopsy suite door, having swapped his thermos for an unlit cigarette, habitually sniffing it under his nose.\n\n\"Autopsy transcript, Case 1107, unidentified male floater,\" Su Tang sat before the recording terminal, her fingers tapping briskly across the keyboard.\n\nPei Yi'an gripped the No. 4 scalpel. The blade hovered momentarily above the deceased's sternum as he whispered, \"Excuse me.\"\n\nThis was his sole ritual before making an incision—a murmur so soft it resembled an inadvertent sigh.\n\nThe cold, razor-sharp blade sliced smoothly down the anterior midline of the neck, dividing the sternum and abdominal wall. Under his masterful technique, the tissue parted cleanly to either side like opening flower petals.\n\n\"No pleural effusion in the thoracic cavity; bilateral lung surfaces are pale and collapsed, verifying that no violent, involuntary water inhalation occurred prior to death,\" Pei Yi'an moved with dazzling speed, the dissecting shears rotating nimbly between his fingers. \"Opening the abdominal cavity. Stand by for olfactory sampling.\"\n\nSu Tang immediately leaned forward with the sampling syringe. As a small three-centimeter incision was made in the gastric wall, a bizarre scent quietly drifted outward.\n\nIt was neither the usual pungent rot nor the acrid burn of gastric acid, but an eerie, sweet fragrance mingling bitter almonds, dried rose petals, and high-purity beeswax.\n\n\"What is that smell?\" Old Zhou, outside the protective glass, straightened abruptly, pulling the cigarette away from his lips. \"Did the guy drink perfume before he died?\"\n\n\"Not perfume,\" Pei Yi'an's brow furrowed slightly for the very first time. He lifted a pair of solid-silver dissecting forceps and slowly probed toward the pyloric antrum of the stomach.\n\nThe tip of the forceps struck something solid, eliciting a faint yet crisp metallic ring—*clink*.\n\nIn that instant, everyone in the autopsy suite held their breath.\n\nPei Yi'an's wrist was rock-steady as he withdrew the forceps millimeter by millimeter. Once the mucus was rinsed away with sterile saline, a mysterious object encased in a layer of translucent, pale-yellow surgical bone wax was finally laid bare under the harsh surgical light.\n\nIt was neither a cyanide capsule nor a smuggled diamond.\n\nIt was an antique, ornate solid brass key, approximately six centimeters in length.\n\nThe bow of the key was meticulously sculpted into the totem of an ouroboros—a winged serpent swallowing its own tail. The serpent's eyes were set with two tiny, dark-red garnets that gleamed with an ominous luster in the frigid light. Along the lateral shank of the key, fine micro-engraving revealed a neat Latin abbreviation and a mysterious four-digit number:\n\n**\"M.S. 1934\"**\n\n\"Good heavens...\" Su Tang sucked in a breath of cold air, her stylus nearly slipping from her trembling fingers. \"Who would swallow an antique key into their stomach?\"\n\n\"It was not swallowed,\" Pei Yi'an clamped the hefty key with his forceps, his gaze more piercing than ever before. \"There is retrograde contusion and hemorrhage along the esophageal mucosa, and the cardiac sphincter is torn. This key was forcibly shoved into the depths of his stomach using tube-feeding equipment while he was moribund and semiconscious.\"\n\nOutside the observation glass, Old Zhou slammed his fist against the frame, sending ripples through the tea in his thermos.\n\n\"He wasn't protecting it, nor was the killer concealing stolen loot,\" Pei Yi'an murmured, the cold glint of the ouroboros mirrored in his lenses. \"The killer treated this human being as a living safe full of riddles, and hid the key to the truth deep inside the victim's corpse.\"\n\nAt that very moment, the morgue clock chimed the top of the hour, its dull, lingering toll echoing through the subterranean depths.\n\nPei Yi'an turned, looking through the glass at Old Zhou's grim countenance, his thin lips parting slightly:\n\n\"Old Zhou, have the field squad ready the car. The dead has delivered his letter to us; now it's our turn to find the door that was locked thirty years ago.\""},{"id":2,"rawContent":"# 第二章：老周的保溫杯與深夜大排檔\n\n十一月的夜雨如期而至，像無數細密的銀針，將濱江市老租界那些斑駁的紅磚牆扎得濕冷透頂。\n\n晚上九點十五分，市局那輛車漆脫落、行駛起來整車都在發出抗議呻吟的老桑塔納警車，慢吞吞地滑過積水氾濫的青石板路，在「三灣大排檔」油膩泛黃的塑膠雨棚前熄了火。\n\n「我再重複一遍，周副隊長。」副駕駛座上的裴以安沒有立刻下車，他將風衣的領口扣得嚴絲合縫，眉頭緊蹙成一道冰冷的山脊，「人體在攝氏八度的潮濕環境下，胃酸分泌會相對增加，但不代表我們需要用高油脂、高嘌呤且來源不明的動物內臟來填補熱量缺口。」\n\n「得了吧，小裴，別整天張嘴閉嘴就跟寫病理報告似的。」老周推開嘎吱作響的車門，一手拎著他那隻萬年不變的大號保溫杯，另一手在空中使勁揮了揮，「解剖了一整天，肚子空得都能聽見回音了。這家『老陳羊肉館』是三十年老字號，那口老湯比你年紀都大！」\n\n「在食品微生物學上，『比我年紀還大』的肉湯通常意味著耐熱性芽孢桿菌與亞硝酸鹽的高度濃縮。」裴以安雖然嘴上無情地批判著，但還是邁開長腿走下了車，並在跨過一灘泛著地溝油彩光的積水時，精準地跨出了整整八十公分。\n\n大排檔的雨棚內熱氣蒸騰，混雜著滾燙的羊肉鮮味、濃烈的大蒜辛辣，以及十幾張摺疊桌周圍食客們划拳碰杯的喧囂聲。\n\n老周極其熟練地挑了張靠牆的空桌，用沾了油漬的抹布在塑料圓凳上隨意一抹，一屁股坐了下來，大聲吆喝道：「老陳！兩碗羊雜麵，多加蒜葉少放辣，再來一盤爆炒腰花、半斤白切羊肉！」\n\n裴以安站在桌旁，整整僵持了七秒鐘。\n\n他從口袋裡掏出一包醫用酒精濕巾，以近乎外科清創手術的嚴謹態度，將面前那張滿是醬油漬的塑料圓凳擦拭了整整三遍，確認表面菌落數可能達到他的心理容忍極限後，才極度勉強地坐了半個臀部。\n\n「小蘇在局裡化驗那層骨蠟，估計半夜才有結果。」老周擰開保溫杯，往嘴裡灌了一口熱茶，神色從剛才的市井痞氣悄然沉了下來，「那把銜尾蛇黃銅鑰匙，你怎麼看？」\n\n裴以安從隨身金屬盒裡倒出一顆薄荷糖，沒有嚼，只是含在舌底，任由極致的冰涼驅散大排檔裡混濁的油煙味。\n\n「黃銅材質，含銅量約為百分之六十五，伴有微量錫與鉛，屬於典型的一九三零年代鑄造工藝。」裴以安修長的手指在桌面上輕輕敲擊，「鑰匙齒痕為七級階梯狀，那是早期『莫里斯·斯坦』（Maurice Stein）機械防盜鎖的專利設計。每一道齒距的公差小於零點零五毫米，現代普通鎖匠根本無法仿製。」\n\n「莫里斯·斯坦？」老周瞇起那雙布滿血絲的眼睛，「就是那個三十年代在濱江舊租界開鐘錶行、後來據說替國民政府中央銀行設計地下金庫的德國猶太機械師？」\n\n「沒錯，鑰匙骨幹上的『M.S. 1934』正是他的個人標識與出廠年份。」裴以安冷靜地分析著，「而另一面的拉丁文縮寫『V.I.T.R.I.O.L.』，是中世紀煉金術士著名的秘語，意思是『參訪地底精微，方能修正重獲秘石』。換成現代人的話來說——這把鑰匙打開的，是一個被埋在地底深處的潘朵拉盒子。」\n\n這時，圍著油漬圍裙的老闆熱情地端上來兩大碗熱氣升騰的羊雜麵，以及一盤滋滋作響、油光鋥亮的爆炒腰花。\n\n「兩位警官慢用！剛出鍋的腰子，嫩著呢！」老闆擦了擦汗，笑呵呵地轉身離去。\n\n老周掰開一雙免洗竹筷，迫不及待地夾了一大塊腰花塞進嘴裡，滿足地嘆了口氣：「人間美味啊！小裴，動筷子啊，看著能飽？」\n\n裴以安面無表情地盯著盤子裡深紅色的腰花，眼神清澈得像是在看解剖切片台。\n\n「新鮮腎臟在加熱至攝氏一百度時，蛋白質迅速凝固，但若爆炒時間不足一分二十秒，中央髓質部分仍會殘留未變性的血紅素。」裴以安推了一下眼鏡，平靜地宣佈，「更重要的是，這隻豬在宰殺前顯然經歷了長期的慢性腎盂腎炎，皮質部分有散在的白色纖維化結節。如果這是在解剖台上，我會建議切除送檢。」\n\n隔壁桌正端著啤酒、大口嚼著腰花的幾名中年男子瞬間石化，嘴裡的肉嚼也不是、嚥也不是，最後驚恐地看了裴以安一眼，默默放下了筷子。\n\n「我說祖宗啊！」老周一口羊肉差點嗆進氣管，哭笑不得地壓低聲音，「吃個夜宵你也能給豬做屍檢！你再多說兩句，老陳這店明天就得被衛生局查封！」\n\n「我只是陳述客觀的病理學事實。」裴以安神色漠然，優雅地抽出筷子，將碗裡所有蔥花以等距排列的方式撥到碗緣，「說回案子。死者的身份，數據庫比對出來了嗎？」\n\n老周擦了擦嘴，臉上的笑意完全褪去，從夾克內袋摸出一份被他揉得皺巴巴的列印簡報，推到裴以安面前。\n\n「比對出來了。林懷遠，三十二歲，華爾街歸國的高級風險精算師，半年前才被聘為濱江新城『瀚海投資集團』的首席財務風控官。」老周壓低了嗓門，「檔案乾淨得像一張白紙，沒有任何前科、沒有仇家，唯一的親人是住在養老院的失智母親。」\n\n「一個每天出入五星級寫字樓、喝手沖咖啡的現代金融高管，」裴以安翻看著簡報上的照片，照片上的男子穿著與屍體上一模一樣的昂貴西裝，眼神自信而銳利，「為什麼會在凌晨三點出現在老船埠，胃裡還塞著一把八十年前的古董金庫鑰匙？」\n\n「而且瀚海集團今天上午剛剛報警，稱林懷遠昨天下午帶走了一份涉及百億私募基金的審計底稿，隨後人間蒸發。」老周的保溫杯在桌面上發出一聲沉悶的撞擊，「更詭異的是，瀚海集團的大股東，正是當年接收了舊租界『明盛洋行』所有地產的陸氏家族。」\n\n裴以安眸光微閃，剛夾起的一片白切羊肉懸在半空。\n\n「三十年代莫里斯·斯坦設計的地下金庫，位置就在現在瀚海集團總部大樓的正下方——也就是舊洋行的老鐘樓地下室。」裴以安的語速極快，思維的齒輪在他腦海中瘋狂咬合，「林懷遠不是被隨機拋屍。兇手是在向瀚海集團、或者說向當年那段歷史的繼承者示威。」\n\n「老鐘樓……」老周喃喃自語，眼神突然飄向了雨棚外漆黑的雨幕。\n\n雨勢越來越大，砸在破舊的塑膠篷頂上，宛如一場急促的行軍鼓點。\n\n就在這時，裴以安放在桌角的私人手機突然震動起來，屏幕上跳動著蘇棠急促的名字。\n\n裴以安接通電話，按下了免提鍵。\n\n「裴老師！周隊！」聽筒那頭傳來蘇棠急促甚至帶著一絲顫抖的聲音，背景裡還伴隨著氣相色譜儀尖銳的報警嗡鳴，「骨蠟的化驗成分出來了！除了高純度石蠟和蜂蠟，表面還提取到了一種极其罕見的植物生物鹼——『劇毒烏頭酸脂』！」\n\n「死因是經胃黏膜吸收的中毒？」老周臉色一沉。\n\n「不！更可怕的是……」蘇棠深吸了一口氣，聲音發緊，「我在那枚黃銅鑰匙內部中空的管柄裡，發現了一截被微型鎢絲纏繞的電子引信！那是一枚微型氣壓遙控感應裝置！」\n\n「兇手在鑰匙裡裝了發信器？」裴以安眼神驟然一縮。\n\n「對！信號在剛剛十秒鐘前被外部激活用戶端連上了！信號源……信號源顯示就在你們附近不到三百米的地方！」\n\n話音未落，大排檔外的老巷口深處，突然傳來一陣刺耳的急剎車聲與金屬撞擊聲！\n\n一道刺目的遠光燈撕裂雨幕，直直打在大排檔薄弱的塑膠棚上，將老周與裴以安的身影森然投射在油膩的泥牆之上。\n\n老周握著保溫杯的手猛然收緊，眼神裡所有的市井渾濁一掃而空，瞬間化為刀鋒般的凜冽。\n\n「小裴，」老周拔出腰間沉甸甸的配槍，嘴角卻扯出一個無比難看的冷笑，「看來這頓羊雜麵，是真沒打算讓我們踏實吃完了。」","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 2: Old Zhou's Thermos & Midnight Food Stalls\n\nThe November night rain arrived on schedule, like countless fine silver needles, soaking the mottled red-brick walls of Binjiang's old concession to a chilling core.\n\nAt 9:15 p.m., the municipal bureau's aged Santana cruiser—its paint peeling and chassis groaning in protest with every rotation of its tires—crept sluggishly over the flooded cobblestones before sputtering to a halt in front of the greasy, yellowed plastic awning of \"Sanwan Food Stalls.\"\n\n\"Let me reiterate, Deputy Captain Zhou.\" In the passenger seat, Pei Yi'an made no immediate move to disembark. He had buttoned the collar of his trench coat up to the chin, his brow furrowed into an icy ridge. \"While a humid environment of eight degrees Celsius does trigger a relative increase in gastric acid secretion, that hardly justifies replenishing caloric deficits with high-fat, high-purine animal viscera of dubious provenance.\"\n\n\"Cut it out, Little Pei. Stop talking all day like you're writing an autopsy report.\" Old Zhou pushed open the squeaking car door, one hand swinging his omnipresent jumbo thermos, the other waving vigorously in the air. \"We've been cutting bodies all day; my stomach is rumbling loudly enough to echo. This 'Old Chen's Mutton House' has been here thirty years—that master broth is older than you!\"\n\n\"In food microbiology, a broth 'older than myself' typically signifies an extreme concentration of heat-resistant endospore bacilli and nitrites.\" Despite his merciless critique, Pei Yi'an stepped out on his long legs, pacing off a stride of precisely eighty centimeters to clear a puddle swirling with iridescent gutter grease.\n\nSteam billowed beneath the awning, dense with the savory richness of boiling mutton, the sharp pungency of crushed garlic, and the boisterous clamor of patrons drinking and playing finger-guessing games around a dozen folding tables.\n\nWith practiced ease, Old Zhou claimed an empty table by the wall. Giving a plastic stool a cursory swipe with a grease-stained rag, he slumped down and hollered, \"Old Chen! Two bowls of mutton offal noodles, heavy on the scallions, light on the chili, a plate of stir-fried kidneys, and half a pound of sliced cold mutton!\"\n\nPei Yi'an remained standing beside the table, paralyzed in place for seven solid seconds.\n\nPulling a pack of medical-grade alcohol wipes from his pocket with the clinical precision of a surgeon performing debridement, he scrubbed the soy-stained plastic stool three full times. Only after judging the surface bacterial colony count had reached the absolute boundary of his psychological endurance did he gingerly rest half of his buttocks on the seat.\n\n\"Little Su is back at the bureau running mass-spec on that bone wax; we probably won't have results till midnight.\" Old Zhou unscrewed his thermos, took a swig of piping-hot tea, and let his street-smart swagger settle into quiet gravity. \"That ouroboros brass key—what do you make of it?\"\n\nPei Yi'an tipped a peppermint lozenge from his tin box. Instead of chewing, he tucked it beneath his tongue, letting the piercing chill dispel the stale frying grease of the night market.\n\n\"Brass alloy, approximately sixty-five percent copper with trace amounts of tin and lead—hallmarks of 1930s metallurgical casting.\" Pei Yi'an tapped the tabletop lightly with his slender fingertips. \"The bitting is stepped across seven distinct levels, a proprietary design of early 'Maurice Stein' mechanical tumbler locks. The tolerance between each tooth is less than 0.05 millimeters; no modern street locksmith could replicate it.\"\n\n\"Maurice Stein?\" Old Zhou narrowed his bloodshot eyes. \"The German-Jewish mechanic who ran a horology shop in the old concession during the thirties, and later supposedly designed the underground vaults for the Nationalist Central Bank?\"\n\n\"Precisely. The 'M.S. 1934' stamped on the shank is his maker's mark and production year.\" Pei Yi'an analyzed coolly. \"On the reverse, the Latin acronym 'V.I.T.R.I.O.L.' is the famous cipher of medieval alchemists: *Visita Interiora Terrae Rectificando Invenies Occultum Lapidem*—visit the interior of the earth, and by purifying you will find the hidden stone. In layman's terms: this key opens a Pandora's box buried deep underground.\"\n\nJust then, the proprietor, wiping his brow with a greasy apron, bustled over with two steaming bowls of mutton offal noodles and a sizzling, glossy plate of stir-fried kidneys.\n\n\"Enjoy, officers! Kidneys fresh off the wok—tender as can be!\" The owner chuckled, wiped his sweat, and turned back to his kitchen.\n\nOld Zhou snapped apart a pair of disposable bamboo chopsticks, snatched a thick piece of kidney, shoved it into his mouth, and exhaled in bliss. \"Pure earthly heaven! Little Pei, pick up your sticks. Staring at it won't fill your belly!\"\n\nPei Yi'an gazed impassively at the deep-crimson kidneys on the platter, his eyes as detached as if examining histological slides.\n\n\"When fresh renal tissue is heated to one hundred degrees Celsius, the proteins coagulate rapidly; however, if stir-fried for under eighty seconds, un-denatured hemoglobin remains in the central medulla.\" Pei Yi'an adjusted his glasses and declared calmly, \"More crucially, this porcine donor evidently suffered from chronic pyelonephritis prior to slaughter, exhibiting scattered white fibrotic nodules across the cortex. Were this on my dissecting table, I would recommend a resection for biopsy.\"\n\nAt the adjacent table, several middle-aged men with beer glasses and mouthfuls of kidney froze instantly. They could neither chew nor swallow, casting terrified glances at Pei Yi'an before quietly setting their chopsticks down.\n\n\"Lord have mercy!\" A bite of mutton nearly lodged in Old Zhou's windpipe as he coughed, hissing in exasperation, \"You're running an autopsy on a pig at a midnight snack stall! Two more sentences out of you, and the health inspectors will shut Old Chen down by sunrise!\"\n\n\"I am merely stating objective pathological facts.\" Expressionless, Pei Yi'an drew his chopsticks and began methodically arranging every scallion ring along the bowl's perimeter at equidistant intervals. \"Returning to the case. Has the database matched the victim's identity?\"\n\nWiping his mouth, all levity vanished from Old Zhou's face. He retrieved a crumpled printout from his jacket's inner breast pocket and slid it across the table.\n\n\"Matched. Lin Huaiyuan, thirty-two, senior risk actuary returning from Wall Street. Appointed Chief Financial Risk Officer at Hanhai Investment Group in the New District six months ago.\" Old Zhou lowered his voice. \"Record as spotless as a blank sheet: no priors, no known feuds. His only living kin is an elderly mother suffering from dementia in a nursing home.\"\n\n\"A modern financial executive who spent his days in five-star office towers drinking pour-over coffee,\" Pei Yi'an scrutinized the photograph—the man wore the identical bespoke suit found on the floater, his gaze sharp and ambitious, \"why would he wash ashore at the old docks at 3 a.m., with an eighty-year-old vault key shoved down his esophagus?\"\n\n\"And Hanhai Group filed a missing person report just this morning, claiming Lin took off yesterday afternoon with the audit papers for a tens-of-billions private equity fund before vanishing off the grid.\" Old Zhou slammed his thermos against the table with a dull thud. \"Even stranger: Hanhai Group's principal shareholder happens to be the Lu family—the very lineage that inherited all properties from the old concession's Mingsheng Trading Company.\"\n\nPei Yi'an's eyes narrowed, a slice of cold mutton suspended in midair between his chopsticks.\n\n\"Maurice Stein's 1930s underground vault is situated directly beneath the current Hanhai Group headquarters—in the subterranean level of the old trading house's historic clocktower.\" Pei Yi'an spoke with rapid fire, mental gears interlocking at breakneck speed. \"Lin Huaiyuan was not dumped at random. The killer is staging a demonstration against Hanhai Group, or rather, against the heirs of that bygone era.\"\n\n\"The old clocktower...\" Old Zhou murmured, his gaze drifting toward the pitch-black curtains of rain beyond the awning.\n\nThe downpour intensified, drumming against the dilapidated plastic canopy like an urgent military march.\n\nAt that moment, Pei Yi'an's phone on the edge of the table vibrated violently, Su Tang's name flashing across the screen.\n\nPei Yi'an answered and tapped speakerphone.\n\n\"Teacher Pei! Captain Zhou!\" Su Tang's voice came through breathless and trembling, punctuated by the shrill warning beeps of a gas chromatograph in the background. \"The bone wax analysis is in! Beyond high-purity paraffin and beeswax, we detected a lethal trace of a rare plant alkaloid—*aconitine ester*!\"\n\n\"Cause of death was poisoning via gastric mucosa absorption?\" Old Zhou's jaw tightened.\n\n\"No! What's far worse is...\" Su Tang took a sharp, jagged breath, her voice tight with terror, \"inside the hollow barrel of that brass key, I found an electronic squib coiled in micro-tungsten wire! It's a miniature barometric remote sensor!\"\n\n\"The killer planted a transmitter inside the key?\" Pei Yi'an's pupils contracted.\n\n\"Yes! And the signal was activated by an external client just ten seconds ago! The transmission source... the ping places it less than three hundred meters from your position!\"\n\nBefore her words could settle, the screech of tires skidding across wet asphalt and a brutal metal crunch echoed from the depths of the rain-drenched alleyway!\n\nA pair of blinding high beams tore through the deluge, pinning their glare straight onto the fragile plastic awning of the food stall, casting the stark silhouettes of Old Zhou and Pei Yi'an against the greasy, soot-stained wall.\n\nOld Zhou's grip on his thermos tightened until his knuckles turned white, every trace of street-wise slackness vanishing in a heartbeat, replaced by the razor-edged fury of a seasoned manhunter.\n\n\"Little Pei,\" Old Zhou drew his heavy service revolver from his hip, a grim, humorless smirk cutting across his mouth, \"looks like they never intended to let us finish our mutton noodles in peace.\""},{"id":3,"rawContent":"# 第三章：三十年前的沉睡保險箱\n\n引擎的暴烈轟鳴在狹窄濕滑的老弄堂裡撕開一道震耳欲聾的裂口。\n\n那輛通體漆黑、卸了車牌的重型越野車宛如一頭狂暴的鋼鐵巨獸，裹挾著刺骨的江風與泥水，徑直朝著大排檔薄弱的塑膠棚撞了過來！\n\n「趴下！」老周怒吼一聲，單手拽住裴以安的風衣後領，猛地將他拖向油膩的磚牆死角，同時另一隻手腕一揚，那隻裝滿滾燙茶水、重達兩斤半的實心不銹鋼保溫杯呼嘯著脫手飛出，化作一道銀色流光。\n\n「砰——嘩啦！」\n\n沉重的保溫杯精準無比地砸碎了越野車的右側大燈，滾燙的枸杞黨參茶水伴隨著防爆玻璃的碎屑四下迸射。\n\n越野車司機顯然沒料到會有如此蠻橫的「非致命性民間防禦武器」，視線受阻之下猛打方向盤，車頭硬生生擦著水泥門柱撞上了路邊的巨型鐵皮垃圾箱，刺耳的金屬扭曲聲瞬間壓過了漫天暴雨。\n\n「周副隊長，根據拋體運動與剛體碰撞公式，您剛才那一記投擲的角度是四十二度，初速約為每秒十四米。」裴以安被按在牆角，鼻樑上的眼鏡微微歪斜，但他神色依舊鎮定得如同在實驗室計量試劑，「但在破壞敵方光學照明系統的同時，您損失了至少三百毫升優質抗氧化草本熱飲，且不可逆地報廢了一隻使用年限超過五年的食品級鋼杯。」\n\n「閉嘴吧祖宗！還有心思給我算拋物線！」老周從腰間拔出六四式手槍，背靠著牆壁大口喘粗氣，花白的鬢角被冷雨澆得透濕，「上車！對方的目標是那把鑰匙，再來兩輛咱們今晚就真得直接躺進你的冷藏櫃了！」\n\n越野車倒車齒輪發出刺耳的尖叫，黑洞洞的槍口已從降下的防彈車窗內探了出來。\n\n老周毫不猶豫地扣動扳機，兩發子彈精準打在對方的輪胎胎壁上，緊接著扯著裴以安鑽進了那輛破舊的桑塔納。老周一腳油門踩到底，老舊的發動機爆發出一陣劇烈的咳嗽聲，噴著黑煙拐進了錯綜複雜的老城死胡同。\n\n二十分鐘後，濱江市雲濱高新區，瀚海投資集團總部大樓。\n\n與舊城區的泥濘油膩截然不同，這座拔地而起七十層的現代摩天大樓由深藍色的雙層鍍膜玻璃與冷軋鋼骨構成，在午夜的雷電映照下，宛如一柄直插烏雲的冰冷手術刀。\n\n大樓的基座，卻保留著一段突兀的暗紅色花崗岩古典立面——那是三十年代舊租界「明盛洋行」的鐘樓舊址。現代資本帝國將它像古董標本一樣包覆在鋼筋混凝土的懷抱中，彰顯著某種不可言說的歷史支配感。\n\n「大樓的安保系統在林懷遠失蹤後全面升級了。」老周將桑塔納熄火在後巷的配電房陰影裡，抖了抖夾克上的雨水，「但他們防得住現代黑客，防不住老子三十年前在舊洋行抓小偷摸熟的通風豎井。」\n\n裴以安整理了一下被雨水打濕的風衣衣領，從口袋裡掏出一雙全新的醫用無菌手套戴上：「莫里斯·斯坦在設計這座建築的地底防禦時，採用的是德式純機械水壓自鎖結構。在那個年代，最好的防盜措施不是電路，而是物理幾何學。」\n\n兩人避開了紅外線感應探頭，順著一條潮濕狹窄的舊式維修通道一路向下。\n\n空氣逐漸變得陰冷沉重。現代大廈地庫那種刺鼻的尾氣與橡膠味被拋在身後，取而代之的是百年磚石特有的青苔腥氣、鐵鏽味，以及一種古老油脂沉澱後的沉悶冷香。\n\n那是時間被幽閉在地下深處發酵的味道。\n\n走過最後一道掛著鏽蝕鐵鎖的鑄鐵拱門，眼前的空間豁然開朗。\n\n那是一間足有兩百平米的八角形地下密室。四周的石牆厚達一米，粗大的承重石柱上雕刻著文藝復興風格的茛苕葉浮雕。而在密室的正中央，赫然矗立著一座高達三米、重達十幾噸的純純黑鐵古典圓形保險庫門。\n\n庫門的核心位置，不是現代指紋密碼盤，而是一個巨大的銅鑄銜尾蛇浮雕圓盤。\n\n蛇頭與蛇尾交疊之處，正中央赫然是一個深邃的垂直鎖眼。\n\n「就是這裡了。」老周舉著手電筒，光柱在斑駁的銅綠上晃動，呼吸不由自主地屏住了，「老洋行當年的地下金庫……三十年沒人打開過了。」\n\n裴以安走上前去，用鑷子從防潮袋中夾出那枚從死者胃袋裡取出的黃銅鑰匙。\n\n「第七級齒痕對應的是內部重力擺錘。」裴以安的指尖輕輕觸摸著冰冷刺骨的鎖孔外沿，側耳貼在庫門厚重的金屬表面上，「莫里斯·斯坦是個偏執狂。他在鎖芯內部安裝了倒懸的自毀硫酸玻璃管，如果扭矩偏差超過兩度，或者順序錯誤，裡面的強酸就會在三秒內融毀所有的聯動齒輪。」\n\n「小裴……你有把握嗎？」老周握著槍的手心微微滲出了冷汗，「要不叫市局的防爆專家過來？」\n\n「防爆專家懂得如何拆解TNT，但他們不懂古典機械師的心跳。」裴以安語調平靜，將薄荷糖在齒間輕輕咬碎，「請保持安靜，聽齒輪咬合的骨傳導聲。」\n\n整座地下室瞬間陷入了死一般的寂靜。\n\n唯有頭頂上方隱約傳來的城市排水管水流聲，以及裴以安沉穩而微弱的呼吸。\n\n黃銅鑰匙緩緩滑入鎖眼，發出一聲清脆而久遠的金屬摩擦聲。\n\n裴以安沒有立刻轉動，而是根據鑰匙骨幹上的拉丁秘語「V.I.T.R.I.O.L.」，按照七個字母對應的音階頻率，將鑰匙向內推入三毫米，向左微旋十五度，停頓兩秒，隨後乾脆利落地向右拉回半格！\n\n「咔噠。」\n\n一聲如同乾枯骨骼復位般的機簧脆響，在庫門深處沉悶地炸開！\n\n緊接著，重達數噸的水壓配重塊在庫門內部轟然滑落，沉睡了近一個世紀的齒輪組開始瘋狂咬合運轉，發出如同遠古鐘錶甦醒般的宏大嗡鳴！\n\n灰塵從門縫中如煙霧般噴湧而出。\n\n巨大的圓形庫門緩緩向外彈開了一道半尺寬的縫隙，一股夾雜著刺鼻防腐化學試劑與陳舊紙張的冷風迎面撲來。\n\n老周與裴以安對視一眼，兩人合力拉開了沉重的鐵門。\n\n手電筒的光柱刺破黑暗，照亮了空曠金庫的中央。\n\n出人意料的是，這座傳說中埋藏著巨額舊時代資產的金庫裡，既沒有堆積如山的金條，也沒有珠寶首飾。\n\n寬闊的花崗岩地面正中央，只孤零零地擺放著一隻由黑色生鐵鑄造的小型手提保險箱。\n\n保險箱並未上鎖，箱蓋半敞著。\n\n裴以安戴著無菌手套，小心翼翼地掀開了沉重的鐵蓋。手電光聚攏在箱底，裡面的三件物品赫然暴露在冰冷的空氣中：\n\n第一件，是一盤直徑十公分、早已停產的三十年代德律風根（Telefunken）開盤磁帶，磁帶邊緣泛著幽暗的金屬光澤；\n\n第二件，是一本用粗麻線裝訂、封面蓋滿了絕密印章的泛黃醫療試驗記錄簿，首頁赫然寫著「新型神經阻斷劑人體耐受試驗（1994）」——而在最後一欄的受試者監護人簽字處，赫然簽著瀚海集團現任董事長「陸崇山」的名字；\n\n而第三件物品，卻是剛剛放進去不久的——\n\n那是一張嶄新的拍立得相片。\n\n相片上，正是昨天才死去的林懷遠。他被粗麻繩死死捆綁在一張金屬手術椅上，雙眼圓睜，瞳孔中倒映著無盡的恐懼。而在相片的背面，用深紅色的油性筆寫著一行優雅得近乎變態的行楷中文：\n\n**「第一份自白書已送達解剖台。第二位審判者正在校準琴弦。——敬呈裴以安法醫」**\n\n地下金庫內的溫度彷彿在這一瞬間驟降到了冰點。\n\n老周看著相片背面的落款，臉色鐵青，嘴唇劇烈地顫抖著：「他……他在直接向你下戰書？！」\n\n裴以安盯著那行紅字，修長的指尖輕輕拂過相片邊緣。在他的鏡片後方，那雙原本清冷孤高的眼眸深處，第一次燃起了一簇鋒利而危險的火焰。\n\n「不，周副隊長。」裴以安直起身，聲音輕得像是一柄出鞘的手術刀，「這不是戰書。這是一份連環解剖邀請函。」","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 3: The Sleeping Safe of Thirty Years\n\nThe violent roar of an engine tore a deafening gash through the narrow, rain-slicked old alleyway.\n\nCompletely matte-black and stripped of its license plates, the heavy-duty off-road vehicle charged forward like a berserk iron beast, hurling biting river winds and slurry straight toward the food stall's fragile plastic canopy!\n\n\"Get down!\" Old Zhou bellowed, grabbing the nape of Pei Yi'an's trench coat with one hand and violently dragging him toward the blind corner of a greasy brick wall. At the same instant, his other wrist flicked, and the solid stainless-steel thermos—brimming with boiling tea and weighing over two pounds—flew whistling from his grip like a silver meteor.\n\n*Crash—shatter!*\n\nThe weighty thermos struck the SUV's right headlight with pinpoint precision, spraying boiling goji and codonopsis tea mixed with shattered explosion-proof glass in every direction.\n\nThe driver had evidently never anticipated meeting such an unhinged \"non-lethal civilian defensive ordinance.\" His vision impaired, he wrenched the steering wheel hard; the fender scraped violently past a concrete doorpost and slammed headlong into a massive corrugated sheet-metal dumpster by the roadside, the screech of crumpling metal drowning out the torrential downpour.\n\n\"Deputy Captain Zhou, according to formulas for projectile motion and rigid-body collisions, your launch angle was forty-two degrees with an initial velocity of approximately fourteen meters per second.\" Pinned against the brick corner with his spectacles knocked askew, Pei Yi'an remained as composed as if titrating reagents in a sterile laboratory. \"However, while successfully disabling the enemy's optical illumination assembly, you squandered at least three hundred milliliters of premium antioxidant herbal hot beverage and irreversibly decommissioned a food-grade steel vessel with over five years of active service.\"\n\n\"Shut your trap, ancestor! You still have the leisure to calculate parabolas for me?!\" Drawing his Type 64 service pistol from his waistband, Old Zhou leaned back against the wall, chest heaving, his greying temples drenched in icy rain. \"Get in the car! Their target is that key; if two more of those show up tonight, we'll be skipping the morgue and moving straight into your refrigeration drawers!\"\n\nThe SUV's reverse gear wailed shrilly, and a pitch-black muzzle emerged from the lowering bulletproof window.\n\nOld Zhou squeezed the trigger without hesitation, planting two rounds cleanly into the sidewalls of the tires. Shoving Pei Yi'an into the battered Santana, Old Zhou stomped the accelerator to the floorboards. The decrepit engine gave a violent series of coughing retches, spewing black exhaust as it whipped into the labyrinth of old-town dead ends.\n\nTwenty minutes later, in the Yunbin Hi-Tech Zone: the corporate headquarters of Hanhai Investment Group.\n\nIn stark contrast to the grime and mud of the historic quarters, this modern seventy-story skyscraper was forged of deep-blue double-glazed curtain walls and cold-rolled structural steel, rising beneath midnight flashes of lightning like an icy scalpel stabbing straight into the storm clouds.\n\nYet the tower's base preserved a jarring neoclassical façade of dark-red granite—the original site of the 1930s concession's \"Mingsheng Trading House\" clocktower. The modern financial empire had encased it within reinforced concrete like an antique specimen, flaunting an unspoken dominion over history.\n\n\"The building's security was upgraded to lockdown status right after Lin Huaiyuan vanished.\" Old Zhou cut the Santana's engine in the shadow of a rear-alley transformer room, shaking the rainwater from his jacket. \"They can keep out modern hackers, but they can't block the ventilation shafts I memorized thirty years ago chasing burglars through the old trading company.\"\n\nStraightening the damp lapels of his trench coat, Pei Yi'an pulled a fresh pair of sterile surgical gloves from his pocket and snapped them on. \"When Maurice Stein engineered this subterranean bastion, he implemented a German purely mechanical hydraulic interlock. In that era, the ultimate security was not electrical circuitry, but physical geometry.\"\n\nSlipping past infrared sensors, the two followed a cramped, damp service duct winding steadily downward.\n\nThe air grew increasingly subterranean and frigid. The biting exhaust fumes and synthetic rubber stench of the high-rise parking garage receded, replaced by the damp mossy tang of century-old masonry, oxidized iron, and the dull, cold perfume of petroleum lubricants settled over decades.\n\nIt was the scent of time itself, fermented in the dark depths of the earth.\n\nPassing through a final cast-iron archway secured with a rusted padlock, the space opened abruptly before them.\n\nIt was an octagonal subterranean chamber spanning two hundred square meters. The perimeter stone walls were a meter thick, with massive load-bearing pillars carved with Renaissance-style acanthus leaf reliefs. And right in the center of the chamber loomed a massive circular vault door of pure dark iron, three meters high and weighing dozens of tons.\n\nIn place of a modern digital keypad or fingerprint scanner, the core of the door was dominated by a colossal cast-bronze relief disk depicting an ouroboros.\n\nWhere the serpent's head clasped its tail in the very center, there lay a deep, vertical keyhole.\n\n\"This is it.\" Old Zhou raised his tactical flashlight, the beam trembling across the mottled green patina as his breath hitched. \"The old trading house's private vault... hasn't been opened in thirty years.\"\n\nStepping forward, Pei Yi'an used forceps to extract the brass key from its moisture-proof evidence pouch.\n\n\"The seventh-tier bitting counterbalances an internal gravity pendulum.\" Pei Yi'an's fingertips brushed gently along the freezing rim of the keyhole as he pressed his ear flat against the vault's dense metal skin. \"Maurice Stein was a clinical obsessive. He mounted an inverted glass vial of concentrated sulfuric acid inside the tumbler; if the torque deviates by more than two degrees or the sequence falters, the acid will melt every interlocking gear within three seconds.\"\n\n\"Little Pei... how sure are you?\" Cold sweat seeped into the palm gripping Old Zhou's sidearm. \"Should we call the bureau's bomb squad?\"\n\n\"Bomb disposal experts know how to defuse TNT, but they cannot hear the heartbeat of a classical master mechanic.\" Pei Yi'an's voice was placid as he bit down on his peppermint lozenge. \"Remain silent, please. Listen to the bone conduction of the tumblers.\"\n\nThe entire subterranean vault sank into absolute, tomb-like stillness.\n\nOnly the muffled rushing of municipal drainage conduits far overhead and Pei Yi'an's steady, shallow breathing remained.\n\nThe brass key slid smoothly into the cylinder, eliciting a crisp, ancient metallic friction.\n\nPei Yi'an did not turn it immediately. Instead, guided by the Latin cipher \"V.I.T.R.I.O.L.\" etched into the shank, he followed the harmonic frequencies of the seven letters: pushing the key three millimeters inward, rotating fifteen degrees counterclockwise, pausing for two seconds, then snapping it back half a notch to the right!\n\n*Click.*\n\nA crisp snap of spring steel, like dried bone resetting into its socket, detonated deep within the door!\n\nImmediately following, hydraulic counterweights weighing several tons plummeted through internal shafts, and a gear train that had slumbered for nearly a century began meshing with ferocity, humming like the waking gears of an ancient cathedral clock!\n\nDust billowed from the seam like steam.\n\nThe colossal circular vault door eased outward by half a foot, unleashing a chilling draft heavy with pungent chemical preservatives and decayed paper.\n\nExchanging a glance, Old Zhou and Pei Yi'an hauled the iron door fully open.\n\nThe flashlight beam pierced the gloom, illuminating the center of the cavernous vault.\n\nContrary to expectation, there were no towering stacks of gold bullion or jewel-encrusted lockboxes in this legendary repository of colonial wealth.\n\nIn the center of the vast granite floor sat a lone, modest portable chest cast from black pig iron.\n\nThe chest was unlocked, its lid ajar.\n\nDonning his sterile gloves, Pei Yi'an carefully hoisted the heavy iron cover. The flashlight pooled into the bottom of the container, revealing three artifacts resting in the cold air:\n\nThe first was a ten-centimeter reel-to-reel magnetic tape from the 1930s—a Telefunken model long out of production, its metallic rim gleaming darkly;\n\nThe second was a yellowed medical trial ledger bound with rough hemp twine, stamped with \"TOP SECRET\" seals, its title page reading: *Human Tolerance Trials of Novel Neuroblocking Agents (1994)*—and in the final column under guardian authorization, the signature read unmistakably: *Lu Chongshan*, the current chairman of Hanhai Group;\n\nBut the third item was modern, placed there only recently—\n\nA brand-new Polaroid print.\n\nThe photograph depicted Lin Huaiyuan, who had died just yesterday. He was bound tightly with rough hemp rope to a metallic operating chair, his eyes wide and dilated with bottomless terror. And on the back of the print, written in deep crimson oil-based ink, was a line of Chinese calligraphy executed with perverse elegance:\n\n**\"The first confession has been delivered to the autopsy table. The second judge is tuning his strings. —Respectfully dedicated to Dr. Pei Yi'an\"**\n\nThe temperature within the underground vault seemed to plunge straight to absolute zero in that instant.\n\nStaring at the inscription on the back of the photograph, Old Zhou's face turned ash-grey, his lips trembling violently. \"He... he's issuing an open challenge directly to you?!\"\n\nPei Yi'an stared fixedly at the crimson brushstrokes, his slender fingers lightly brushing the edge of the Polaroid. Behind his lenses, deep within those eyes that were normally so detached and clinical, a sharp, dangerous flame ignited for the very first time.\n\n\"No, Deputy Captain Zhou.\" Pei Yi'an straightened, his voice whisper-soft like an unsheathed scalpel. \"This is no challenge. This is an invitation to a serial autopsy.\""},{"id":4,"rawContent":"# 第四章：雨幕中的江邊舊船廠\n\n凌晨三點半，濱江市北岸的工業荒原沉浸在一片死寂與暴雨之中。\n\n這裡曾是整座城市最繁忙的「東江造船廠」，如今只剩下數十座高聳如鋼鐵巨獸的生鏽門座式起重機，在低垂的鉛灰色雲層下無聲佇立，宛如一排排被時代遺棄的受刑架。\n\n在局裡那場令人窒息的午夜問訊中，瀚海集團董事長陸崇山雖然憑藉龐大的律師團對三十年前的試驗記錄三緘其口，但他發白的嘴唇與顫抖的指尖，早已出賣了他內心深處的崩潰。而蘇棠對那張拍立得相片的微量痕跡分析，更是鎖定了致命破局點——背景金屬板上剝落的防銹紅丹漆、鉚釘排列密度，以及林懷遠鞋底採樣到的特殊淡水藤壺孢子，全部指向了這座廢棄了整整十二年的老船廠。\n\n老桑塔納警車碾碎滿地的碎石與積水，在二號乾塢生鏽的鐵絲網外緩緩停下。\n\n「我新換的保溫杯，十塊錢在通宵雜貨鋪隨便買的便宜貨。」老周推開車門，右手端著一隻印著鮮紅喜字的雙層鐵皮保溫桶，嘴裡叼著沒點著的煙，一臉肉痛地嘆氣，「既沒沉重的手感，保溫性能也差勁透頂。小裴，要是今晚再遇到拿車撞人的亡命徒，這玩意兒扔出去估計連人家的車漆都砸不掉一塊。」\n\n「從材料力學角度來看，薄壁低碳鋼板在受衝擊時會發生塑性形變，能量吸收率確實遠低於奧氏體不銹鋼。」裴以安撐開一柄黑色的長柄雨傘，跨過泥濘的車轍，雪白的手術乳膠手套在黑暗中分外扎眼，「不過周副隊長，比起您對茶具的哀悼，我更建議您注意呼吸節奏——周圍空氣中的氯離子濃度高達每立方米二十毫克，長期暴露會加速呼吸道黏膜的慢性纖維化。」\n\n「得了，這鬼地方連鬼都不願意來，就咱倆跟兩條落湯雞似的在這裡聞鐵鏽。」老周嘴上雖然沒個正經，但拔出腰間佩槍的動作卻敏捷得像一隻獵豹，保險機簧「咔嗒」一聲在雨中輕響。\n\n兩人踩著淹沒腳踝的泥水，沿著乾塢斑駁的鐵梯一路向下。\n\n巨大的船塢深達十幾米，兩側是佈滿貝殼與青苔的水泥高牆，雨水從上方如瀑布般傾瀉而下，將整座乾塢灌注成一座回音巨大的鋼鐵深淵。\n\n手電筒的雪白光柱在黑暗中晃動，刺破重重雨幕，最終定格在乾塢最深處的一座懸空鐵皮調度室前。\n\n調度室的鐵門半掩著，門框上有一道新鮮的撬痕。\n\n裴以安用戴著手套的手指輕輕推開鐵門，伴隨著一聲乾澀刺耳的金屬摩擦聲，屋內的空氣撲面而來。\n\n沒有海水的腥味，也沒有陳舊機油的氣味。\n\n那是一股濃郁而詭異的混合氣息——福馬林、高純度松香，以及木質大提琴琴弦受潮後特有的沉悶木香。\n\n手電筒的光束在狹小的調度室內一掃，老周的瞳孔猛地收縮，倒吸了一口涼氣。\n\n在房間的正中央，赫然擺放著那張出現在拍立得相片裡的金屬手術椅！\n\n椅背與扶手上的粗麻繩已經被利刃割斷，地面上殘留著幾滴早已發黑凝固的暗紅色血跡。而在手術椅前方的鐵皮操作台上，整齊地擺放著一隻正在以極其緩慢的速度擺動的機械節拍器。\n\n「嗒……嗒……嗒……」\n\n單調而沉悶的敲擊聲在密閉的鐵皮屋裡迴盪，每隔兩秒響起一次，節奏精準得令人窒息。\n\n「小裴，別過去！」老周猛地伸手攔住裴以安，目光死死盯著操作台下方，「你看地面！」\n\n只見水泥地面上，縱橫交錯地拉著數十根細如髮絲的鋼絲琴弦。琴弦的一端固定在操作台的節拍器發條上，另一端則隱沒在房間四周的鐵皮夾層深處，在手電光下泛著幽冷的鋼藍色光澤。\n\n「這不是爆炸引信，」裴以安停下腳步，神情平靜得近乎超然，甚至微微俯下身去觀察琴弦的張力與規格，「這是高張力的羊腸金屬纏弦，通常用於演奏級大提琴的C弦。兇手用節拍器的機械擺錘作為張力平衡器，只要有人踩斷任何一根弦，失去平衡的擺錘就會觸發暗格裡的機關。」\n\n裴以安從風衣內袋中掏出那枚訂製的純銀解剖鑷，手指穩如磐石，輕輕夾住其中一根鋼絲的連接點，藉著手電筒的光芒順藤摸瓜。\n\n在操作台的正後方，鏽跡斑斑的鐵皮牆面上，赫然被人用鋒利的鋼鑽生生刻出了一幅巨大的文藝復興時期人體解剖圖——《維特魯威人》。\n\n只不過，畫像中男子的頭顱被替換成了一把泣血的大提琴，而在畫像的心臟部位，嵌入了一張浸透了松香水的小型樂譜殘頁。\n\n樂譜的正上方，用鮮紅的印泥蓋著一行清晰的漢字與一個名字：\n\n**「第二樂章：獻給失聰的聽審者——濱江愛樂樂團首席大提琴家，陸思遠。」**\n\n「陸思遠？」老周咬牙切齒地念出這個名字，「陸崇山的親侄子，濱江市最有名的青年大提琴演奏家！」\n\n「不僅如此。」裴以安收起鑷子，鏡片深處的光芒無比冷冽，「在三十年前那份『神經阻斷劑人體試驗』記錄的附錄中，受試者名單的編號07，正是一名年僅四歲、患有先天性聽神經發育不全的幼童。他的法定監護人欄位上，赫然寫著陸思遠父親的名字。」\n\n「這是一場跨越三十年、針對陸氏家族血親的精確復仇清算！」老周猛地轉身，望向窗外狂暴的雨幕。\n\n就在這時，調度室外面的泥濘空地上，突然傳來了一聲極其微弱但清晰的腳步聲——\n\n「啪嗒。」\n\n那是特質橡膠靴踩碎積水與爛泥的聲音。\n\n老周與裴以安瞬間屏住了呼吸，整座調度室內，只剩下那個機械節拍器在不知疲倦地發出冰冷的「嗒、嗒」聲。\n\n窗外的暴風雨中，一道撐著黑色大傘的修長陰影，正穿過鐵絲網的破口，踩著滿地鋼鐵廢墟，緩緩朝著這座乾塢走來。\n\n老周雙手持槍抵住門框，眼神冰冷如鐵；而裴以安則緩緩推了推鼻樑上的眼鏡，舌尖將最後一點薄荷糖的極致冰涼，狠狠壓入了喉嚨深處。","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 4: The Old Shipyard in the Rain\n\nAt 3:30 a.m., the industrial wasteland on Binjiang's north bank lay submerged in dead silence and torrential rain.\n\nOnce the city's most bustling hub, the \"East River Shipyard\" now retained only dozens of rusted portal gantry cranes towering like iron behemoths, standing mutely beneath low-hanging leaden clouds like a colonnade of scaffolds discarded by time.\n\nDuring that suffocating midnight interrogation at headquarters, though Hanhai Group Chairman Lu Chongshan had hidden behind an army of attorneys to maintain strict silence regarding the thirty-year-old clinical trial records, his pale lips and trembling fingertips had long betrayed the collapse deep within his soul. Furthermore, Su Tang's trace analysis of the Polaroid print had pinpointed the fatal breakthrough—flaking red-lead anti-corrosive primer on the background metal plates, the specific rivet pitch, and freshwater barnacle spores sampled from Lin Huaiyuan's soles all converged on this shipyard, abandoned for twelve long years.\n\nThe aged Santana police cruiser crunched through gravel and pooling rainwater, idling to a halt outside the rusted chain-link fence of Dry Dock No. 2.\n\n\"My replacement thermos—ten bucks at an all-night bodega, cheap piece of junk.\" Old Zhou kicked open the car door, clutching in his right hand a double-walled tin jug stamped with a bright-red double-happiness character, an unlit cigarette dangling from his lips as he groaned in agony. \"Lacks all heft, and its thermal insulation is downright miserable. Little Pei, if another madman tries to ram us with an SUV tonight, chucking this thing probably won't even scratch his paint.\"\n\n\"From the perspective of materials mechanics, thin-walled low-carbon sheet steel undergoes severe plastic deformation upon impact, yielding an energy absorption rate far inferior to austenitic stainless steel.\" Unfurling a long-handled black umbrella, Pei Yi'an stepped across the muddy ruts, his snowy surgical latex gloves starkly prominent against the gloom. \"However, Deputy Captain Zhou, rather than lamenting your teaware, I strongly advise regulating your respiration—the atmospheric chloride ion concentration here reaches twenty milligrams per cubic meter. Chronic exposure accelerates pulmonary mucosal fibrosis.\"\n\n\"Forget it. Even ghosts wouldn't visit this godforsaken swamp, yet here the two of us are, sniffing rust like a pair of drowned rats.\" Despite his irreverent banter, Old Zhou unholstered his service revolver with the fluid grace of a stalking panther, the hammer clicking back softly into the downpour.\n\nWading through ankle-deep slurry, the two descended along the mottled iron staircase of the dry dock.\n\nThe cavernous dock plunged over ten meters down, flanking them with towering concrete retaining walls encrusted in barnacles and moss. Rain cascaded from above like a waterfall, turning the entire basin into a booming abyss of steel echoes.\n\nThe snowy beam of the tactical flashlight cut through dense sheets of rain, sweeping across the dark until it locked onto a suspended sheet-metal dispatch cabin at the innermost recess of the dock.\n\nThe cabin's iron door hung slightly ajar, a fresh pry mark scarring the latch.\n\nPei Yi'an nudged the iron door open with a gloved finger. With a dry, screeching grating of rusted hinges, the interior air surged out to meet them.\n\nNeither the brackish tang of the river nor the reek of stale engine grease awaited them.\n\nInstead, it was an eerie, rich cocktail of scents—formalin, high-purity rosin, and the heavy, woody perfume characteristic of damp cello strings.\n\nAs the flashlight beam swept across the cramped cabin, Old Zhou's pupils shrank, his breath catching violently in his throat.\n\nIn the exact center of the room stood the metal operating chair seen in the Polaroid!\n\nThe thick hemp ropes binding the backrest and armrests had been severed with a blade, leaving several spattered drops of darkened, congealed blood across the floorboards. On the iron console directly before the chair, a mechanical clockwork metronome clicked back and forth at an agonizingly measured pace.\n\n*Tick... tick... tick...*\n\nThe monotonous, hollow cadence reverberated inside the sealed metal chamber, striking once every two seconds with suffocating precision.\n\n\"Little Pei, don't move!\" Old Zhou clamped a hand onto Pei Yi'an's shoulder, his eyes fixed on the floor beneath the console. \"Look at the deck!\"\n\nCrisscrossing the concrete floor were dozens of steel strings as fine as human hairs. One end of each string anchored to the metronome's mainspring on the console, while the other ends disappeared into the corrugated wall partitions, glinting with a cold, steely-blue sheen under the flashlight beam.\n\n\"This is no explosive trigger,\" Pei Yi'an halted, his demeanor unnervingly calm as he leaned forward to inspect the tension and gauge of the wire. \"These are high-tension gut-core wound strings, typically reserved for the C-string of a concert-grade cello. The killer utilized the metronome's pendulum as a kinetic counterbalance. Sever any single string, and the upset equilibrium will trip the mechanism concealed within the walls.\"\n\nReaching into his breast pocket for his custom silver forceps, Pei Yi'an clamped the junction of a steel wire with unwavering fingers, tracing the connection under the flashlight's illumination.\n\nDirectly behind the console, engraved deep into the rusted iron sheeting with a hardened steel drill, was a massive Renaissance anatomical sketch—*The Vitruvian Man*.\n\nExcept the figure's head had been supplanted by a weeping cello, and embedded within its cardiac region was a miniature scrap of sheet music saturated in turpentine and rosin.\n\nPrinted across the header in crimson stamp-pad ink was a row of Chinese characters accompanying a prominent name:\n\n**\"Movement Two: Dedicated to the Deaf Juror—Principal Cellist of the Binjiang Philharmonic, Lu Siyuan.\"**\n\n\"Lu Siyuan?\" Old Zhou ground out the name through clenched teeth. \"Lu Chongshan's nephew—Binjiang's most celebrated young cellist!\"\n\n\"More than that.\" Tucking his forceps away, the glint behind Pei Yi'an's glasses turned razor-sharp. \"In the appendix to that thirty-year-old neuroblocking agent clinical trial, Subject 07 was a four-year-old child suffering from congenital auditory nerve hypoplasia. The legal guardian signed in the ledger was none other than Lu Siyuan's father.\"\n\n\"A calculated, thirty-year vendetta targeting the Lu family's bloodline!\" Old Zhou spun toward the tempest outside the window.\n\nAt that precise moment, from the muddy clearing outside the dispatch cabin, a faint yet distinct footstep landed—\n\n*Squelch.*\n\nThe unmistakable suction of heavy rubber boots pressing into wet mire.\n\nOld Zhou and Pei Yi'an froze instantly, leaving only the mechanical metronome inside the cabin to measure the silence with its relentless, frozen *tick, tick*.\n\nOut in the rain, a tall, slender silhouette beneath a massive black umbrella emerged through the torn chain-link fence, stepping across the industrial graveyard toward the dry dock.\n\nGripping his sidearm against the doorframe, Old Zhou's gaze hardened into cold steel; while Pei Yi'an adjusted his silver spectacles, his tongue pressing the final, biting chill of his peppermint lozenge deep into his throat."},{"id":5,"rawContent":"# 第五章：死者未發出的遺言\n\n暴雨如注，打在乾塢破敗的波形鐵皮瓦上，發出宛如千軍萬馬奔襲般的沉悶鼓噪。\n\n調度室門外那雙泥濘的橡膠靴在距離門檻三步遠的地方停住了。\n\n老周雙手持槍，後背緊貼著冰冷的鐵門框，渾身肌肉繃緊如滿月之弓。就在那柄巨大的黑傘傘沿微微下壓、一隻蒼白消瘦的手正欲推門的剎那，老周猛然一個側步跨出，槍口黑洞洞地直抵對方的眉心！\n\n「別動！市局刑偵隊！」老周一聲暴喝，聲如驚雷。\n\n黑傘猛地向後一仰，傘骨在狂風中劇烈翻卷。借著手電筒慘白刺目的光柱，出現在槍口下的並非窮兇極惡的悍匪，而是一個身穿純黑修身長大衣、臉色白得近乎透明的年輕男人。\n\n他大約二十七八歲，雙手緊緊抱著一隻沉重的航空防震大提琴硬盒，精緻的五官在暴雨中劇烈抽搐，嘴唇烏青，整個人抖得像是一片在深秋寒風中即將飄落的枯葉。\n\n「別……別開槍！我是陸思遠！」年輕人嘶啞地喊道，聲音裡帶著撕心裂肺的哭腔，「是那個人讓我來的……他說如果我在凌晨四點前趕不到這個乾塢，我就永遠別想再拉琴了！」\n\n裴以安從懸空調度室內緩步走出，黑色的長柄雨傘在身前穩穩撐開，冰冷的目光掠過陸思遠懷中的琴盒，隨後落在他劇烈顫抖的雙手上。\n\n「雙手尺側腕屈肌劇烈痙攣，指尖伴有典型的神經源性震顫。」裴以安平靜地陳述道，甚至沒有多看那黑洞洞的槍口一眼，「陸先生，對於一名享譽國際的青年大提琴演奏家來說，將您的前臂長時間暴露在攝氏六度的潮濕低溫下，其職業自殺性質不亞於吞服氰化物。」\n\n陸思遠愣愣地看著這個氣質清冷如冰雕般的法醫，彷彿在這一瞬間忘記了死亡的恐懼：「你……你怎麼知道……」\n\n「進來，把傘收了，但千萬別碰到地上的鋼絲琴弦。」老周收起配槍，警惕地掃視了一眼漆黑無人的荒涼船廠，一把將陸思遠拽進了懸空調度室。\n\n當手電光照亮鐵壁上那幅被刻成泣血大提琴的《維特魯威人》，以及下方那張寫著他名字的樂譜殘頁時，陸思遠雙腿一軟，整個人重重地跪倒在地，懷裡的琴盒發出一聲沉悶的震盪。\n\n「他果然找來了……他回來了……三十年前的報應，終於輪到我們家了……」陸思遠將頭埋在冰冷的手術椅金屬邊緣，眼淚混合著冰冷的雨水肆意淌落。\n\n「三十年前到底發生了什麼？」老周一把揪住陸思遠的衣領，聲音壓抑著狂暴的怒火，「那個在背後操控一切的『擺渡人』究竟是誰？他為什麼要把三十年前的磁帶與林懷遠的屍體綁在一起？！」\n\n「我不知道他的名字……真的不知道！」陸思遠痛苦地抱住腦袋，「我只知道，我父親三十年前根本不是死於突發心肌梗塞，他是自殺的！在他死前的那天晚上，他瘋狂地砸毀了家裡所有的音響與琴譜，嘴裡一直重複著一句話——『我們把活人當成小白鼠，把死者當成不說話的垃圾，這條江水遲早會把所有的罪惡沖刷回來的！』」\n\n裴以安沒有打斷陸思遠崩潰的哭喊，他戴著無菌手套的手從隨身勘驗箱中取出了那台從市局物證室緊急調來的便攜式精密音訊還原儀。\n\n在操作台那隻仍在不知疲倦擺動的機械節拍器旁，裴以安將那盤從瀚海集團地下金庫取出的三十年代德律風根開盤磁帶，小心翼翼地卡入了讀取轉軸。\n\n「磁帶表面沉積了厚達七微米的碳酸鈣結晶與氧化鐵粉末，但聚酯基帶並未完全降解。」裴以安的手指在調節旋鈕上精準撥動，微調著雷射磁頭的掃描頻率，「死者無法用聲帶發出聲音，但磁粉記錄了三十年前最後一秒的空氣振動。」\n\n「嗒……嗒……嗒……」\n\n節拍器的單調聲響中，音訊還原儀的信號指示燈從刺目的警報紅色，緩緩轉變為平穩的翠綠色。\n\n一陣刺耳的電流雜音如沙暴般在封閉的鐵皮屋內炸響，隨後，三十年前被深埋在地底深處的冰冷人聲，穿透了漫長的時光迷霧，幽然響起：\n\n『……崇山，你瘋了！這項神經阻斷劑的臨床毒性根本沒有代謝乾淨！你把劑量私自加到三倍，07號孩子的大腦聽覺中樞已經出現了不可逆的病變！你這是謀殺！』\n\n那是一個年輕而清澈的男子嗓音，憤怒中帶著無法遏制的絕望。\n\n緊接著，音訊裡傳來了另一個無比低沉、陰冷卻又無比熟悉的成年男子聲音——正是瀚海集團現任董事長、陸思遠的伯父陸崇山三十年前的聲音：\n\n『林清源博士，別忘了是誰資助了你的實驗室。明盛洋行的地產改制就在下個月，這批新藥專利是我們拿到外資信貸唯一的抵押品！至於那個孩子……他本來就是個聾子，能為科學做出貢獻是他唯一的價值！』\n\n『畜生！我要去衛理公會醫學院揭發你！我要把所有的試驗底稿公之於眾！』\n\n『揭發我？走出這個船廠的二號乾塢，你覺得還有人能聽見你的聲音嗎？』\n\n錄音帶裡傳來一陣劇烈的肢體扭打聲、金屬器械砸落在水泥地面的轟鳴，以及人體被重物擊中後沉悶的窒息喘息。\n\n最後，是沉重的肉體破開江水的落水巨響——「噗通！」\n\n錄音戛然而止，唯餘下一片沙沙的空白磁噪。\n\n整座調度室陷入了死一般的冰冷寂靜。\n\n陸思遠癱軟在地上，面如死灰；老周緊握著雙拳，關節因為用力過度而泛出滲人的慘白。\n\n「林清源……」老周從牙縫中擠出這三個字，「三十年前離奇失蹤的舊租界市立醫院病理科主任……林懷遠的親生父親！」\n\n「這就是所有的閉環鏈條。」裴以安切斷電源，將磁帶取下，鏡片後那雙銳利的眼眸彷彿看穿了一切因果，「三十年前，陸崇山在二號乾塢殺害了林清源博士，偽裝成投江自盡，並利用掠奪來的藥物專利與地產建立了瀚海帝國；三十年後，林清源的兒子林懷遠查明了真相，卻在即將揭露黑幕前夕，被兇手以同樣的手段殺死並拋屍江中。」\n\n「等等……」老周敏銳地察覺到了異樣，「如果林懷遠是復仇者，那殺害林懷遠的『擺渡人』又是誰？他既然是在替三十年前的冤魂復仇，為什麼連林博士唯一的兒子也要殺？！」\n\n「因為林懷遠妥協了。」\n\n一道蒼老而優雅的聲音，毫無徵兆地從調度室角落那隻靜默的對講機中緩緩傳出。\n\n對講機的紅燈劇烈閃爍，揚聲器裡伴隨著狂風驟雨的呼嘯，以及一陣宛如死神吟唱般低沉悠揚的大提琴撥弦聲：\n\n「林懷遠拿著底稿向陸崇山索要了三千萬封口費，他背叛了他父親高潔的靈魂，把正義當成了討價還價的籌碼。裴法醫，我說過，死者比活人更有禮貌——因為死者不會為了骯髒的紙幣，向殺父仇人屈膝下跪。」\n\n老周猛地抓起對講機，怒吼道：「你是誰？！你到底在哪裡？！」\n\n對講機那頭傳來一聲極輕的冷笑，宛如手術刀鋒擦過玻璃：\n\n「老周副隊長，何必這麼心急？看一看你們腳下吧——第三首安魂曲的計時器，已經在陸思遠先生踏進這間屋子的那一刻，正式開始倒計時了。」","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 5: The Unspoken Last Words\n\nThe torrential downpour hammered relentlessly against the dilapidated corrugated iron roof of the dry dock, producing a muffled roar like the thundering stampede of ten thousand steeds.\n\nOutside the dispatch cabin door, the muddy rubber boots halted three paces short of the threshold.\n\nGripping his sidearm in both hands, Old Zhou pressed his back flush against the frigid iron doorframe, every sinew in his body coiled like a drawn recurve bow. Just as the brim of the massive black umbrella tilted slightly and a pale, gaunt hand reached out to push the door, Old Zhou lunged laterally, leveling the dark muzzle square between the stranger's eyebrows!\n\n\"Don't move! Municipal Criminal Investigation Detachment!\" Old Zhou barked, his voice detonating like a thunderclap.\n\nThe black umbrella jerked violently backward, its ribs thrashing wildly in the tempest. Illuminated by the glaring white cone of the tactical flashlight, the figure caught in the crosshairs was no hardened, desperate thug, but a young man clad in a tailored black overcoat, his complexion translucent with terror.\n\nHe appeared roughly twenty-seven or twenty-eight years old, his arms clutching a heavy, shockproof aeronautical hardcase for a cello, his refined features contorted in the pelting rain, his lips bruised blue, shuddering like a solitary withered leaf on the verge of falling in late autumn's gale.\n\n\"Don't... don't shoot! I'm Lu Siyuan!\" the youth cried hoarsely, a heart-wrenching sob cracking in his throat. \"That person sent me here... he said if I didn't reach this dry dock before 4:00 a.m., I would never touch a cello again in my life!\"\n\nPei Yi'an stepped slowly out from the suspended dispatch cabin, his long-handled black umbrella held rock-steady before him, his clinical gaze skimming past the cello case in Lu Siyuan's arms before fixing upon the youth's violently trembling hands.\n\n\"Severe spasticity in the flexor carpi ulnaris bilaterally, accompanied by classic neurogenic tremors in the distal digits.\" Pei Yi'an stated impassively, not sparing so much as a glance at the leveled firearm. \"Mr. Lu, for an internationally renowned young concert cellist, exposing your forearms to a damp, frigid environment of six degrees Celsius for an extended period constitutes an act of professional suicide scarcely different from ingesting potassium cyanide.\"\n\nLu Siyuan stared blankly at this forensic pathologist who possessed the cold demeanor of an ice sculpture, as if the primal dread of death had momentarily deserted him in sheer bafflement: \"You... how do you know...\"\n\n\"Get inside, fold your umbrella, and whatever you do, don't trip the steel cello strings on the deck.\" Holstering his revolver, Old Zhou swept a watchful gaze across the desolate, pitch-black shipyard before yanking Lu Siyuan across the threshold into the suspended dispatch cabin.\n\nWhen the beam of the flashlight illuminated the *Vitruvian Man* carved into the iron wall with a weeping cello, alongside the scrap of sheet music bearing his name directly beneath it, Lu Siyuan's knees liquefied, collapsing heavily to the deck as his cello case struck the floor with a dull, hollow boom.\n\n\"He really found me... he came back... the retribution from thirty years ago has finally fallen upon our house...\" Lu Siyuan buried his face against the freezing metal lip of the surgical chair, tears mingling freely with icy rainwater and streaming down his cheeks.\n\n\"What in the hell happened thirty years ago?\" Old Zhou seized Lu Siyuan by the collar, his voice laced with suffocating, smoldering fury. \"Who is this 'Ferryman' pulling all the strings from the shadows?! Why did he tie that thirty-year-old tape to Lin Huaiyuan's corpse?!\"\n\n\"I don't know his name... I swear I don't!\" Lu Siyuan clutched his head in agony. \"All I know is that my father didn't die of a sudden myocardial infarction thirty years ago—he committed suicide! On the night before he took his life, he smashed every stereo and music score in our house in a manic fit, repeating the exact same words over and over: *'We treated living people like lab rats, and we treated the dead like voiceless garbage; sooner or later, this river will wash all the blood and sin back to our doorstep!'*\"\n\nPei Yi'an did not interrupt Lu Siyuan's broken lamentation. Slipping on fresh sterile gloves, he retrieved a portable precision audio restoration deck from his forensic kit—equipment dispatched via emergency courier from the municipal bureau's evidence lab.\n\nBeside the mechanical clockwork metronome on the console that still swung with tireless rhythm, Pei Yi'an gingerly mounted the 1930s Telefunken reel-to-reel magnetic tape—recovered from the Hanhai Group subterranean vault—onto the drive spindles.\n\n\"A layer of calcium carbonate crystals and ferric oxide dust seven micrometers thick has settled across the tape surface, yet the polyester base remains structurally uncompromised.\" Pei Yi'an adjusted the calibrated dials with micro-metric precision, tuning the scanning frequency of the laser playback head. \"The dead cannot produce sound with their vocal cords, but magnetic powder faithfully preserves the final vibrations of the air from thirty years ago.\"\n\n*Tick... tick... tick...*\n\nAmid the metronome's sterile cadence, the restoration deck's signal indicator shifted slowly from a cautionary amber-red to a serene emerald green.\n\nA blast of electrical static hissed through the sealed sheet-metal chamber like a sandstorm. Then, a cold, long-buried human voice—preserved from the subterranean depths thirty years prior—pierced through the foggy corridors of time, echoing with haunting clarity:\n\n*\"Chongshan, have you lost your mind?! The clinical neurotoxicity of this blocking agent hasn't cleared baseline metabolism! You tripled the dosage unauthorized, and Subject 07's auditory cortex has suffered irreversible neurological damage! This is murder!\"*\n\nIt was the voice of a young, articulate man, vibrating with indignation and insurmountable despair.\n\nImmediately following, another deep, chilled, yet unmistakably familiar adult voice rolled through the speaker—the voice of Lu Chongshan, now chairman of Hanhai Group, recorded thirty years in his youth:\n\n*\"Dr. Lin Qingyuan, don't forget whose capital financed your laboratory. The privatization restructuring of Mingsheng Trading House takes place next month, and these novel drug patents are our sole collateral for foreign credit lines! As for that child... he was born deaf anyway. Contributing to medical science is the only worth his existence will ever offer!\"*\n\n*\"You monster! I will expose you to the Methodist College of Medicine! I will drag every single trial protocol and audit draft into the broad light of day!\"*\n\n*\"Expose me? Once you walk out of Dry Dock Number Two in this shipyard, do you truly believe anyone alive will ever hear your voice again?\"*\n\nThe audio dissolved into violent physical scuffling, the clang of metallic instruments crashing across concrete, and the muffled, choked gasps of a human body absorbing blunt trauma.\n\nFinally, there came the monstrous, cavernous impact of dead weight cleaving the river's surface—*Splash!*\n\nThe recording terminated abruptly, leaving only the dry hiss of blank magnetic tape.\n\nAbsolute, subterranean chill settled over the dispatch cabin.\n\nLu Siyuan slumped limp against the floor, his face drained of all color; Old Zhou's fists were clenched so violently that his knuckles gleamed a terrifying, bloodless white.\n\n\"Lin Qingyuan...\" Old Zhou ground the words past his teeth. \"The Chief of Pathology at the old Concession Municipal Hospital who vanished without a trace thirty years ago... Lin Huaiyuan's biological father!\"\n\n\"This closes the entire causal loop.\" Pei Yi'an powered down the unit and removed the spool, the razor-sharp gaze behind his lenses piercing straight to the philosophical core. \"Thirty years ago, Lu Chongshan murdered Dr. Lin Qingyuan in Dry Dock Number Two, staged it as a suicidal leap into the river, and built his Hanhai empire upon stolen pharmaceuticals and usurped real estate. Thirty years later, Lin's son Lin Huaiyuan unearthed the truth—yet on the very eve of exposing the conspiracy, he was murdered and dumped into the identical river by the exact same methodology.\"\n\n\"Wait a second...\" Old Zhou's veteran instincts caught a fatal dissonance. \"If Lin Huaiyuan was the avenger, then who is this 'Ferryman' hunting in the shadows? If he's executing vengeance on behalf of a ghost from thirty years ago, why would he slaughter Dr. Lin's only son as well?!\"\n\n\"Because Lin Huaiyuan compromised.\"\n\nAn aged, impeccably cultured voice floated softly from a silent handheld transceiver resting in the corner of the cabin.\n\nThe transceiver's red LED flashed furiously, the speaker carrying the wail of the tempest outside along with the deep, sonorous plucking of cello pizzicato—a melody that sounded like the grim hymn of the reaper himself:\n\n\"Lin Huaiyuan leveraged the audit records to extort thirty million in hush money from Lu Chongshan. He betrayed the noble soul of his father, reducing justice to a commodity for barter. Dr. Pei, as I once stated, the dead are far more polite than the living—for the dead never kneel before their father's murderer for soiled scraps of paper currency.\"\n\nSnatching the transceiver, Old Zhou roared into the grille: \"Who are you?! Where the hell are you hiding?!\"\n\nA soft, chilling chuckle slipped from the speaker, sounding like the scrape of a scalpel along polished glass:\n\n\"Deputy Captain Zhou, why so impatient? Look beneath your feet—the timer for the Third Requiem commenced the exact second Mr. Lu Siyuan stepped across your threshold.\""},{"id":6,"rawContent":"# 第六章：鎖眼裡的警告信\n\n對講機裡的冷笑聲方落，懸空調度室鐵壁深處的機簧便爆發出一陣令人牙酸的金屬絞動聲。\n\n「轟隆——」\n\n整座懸空的鐵皮屋猛烈震顫了一下，原本每兩秒擺動一次的機械節拍器突然瘋狂加速，指針在刻度盤上劃出道道殘影，發出宛如毒蛇吐信般急促的「嗒嗒嗒嗒」聲！\n\n「老周！腳下！」裴以安厲聲喝道。\n\n只見調度室四周的鐵皮夾層內，並未噴出致命的毒氣或火焰，而是傳來了水流撕裂閥門的狂暴咆哮。透過地板縫隙望去，二號乾塢底部那兩扇重達數十噸、原本早已廢棄閉合的防洪鐵閘門，竟被隱蔽的液壓機關強行頂開了一道三尺寬的豁口！\n\n滾滾長江水裹挾著刺骨的江風與黑黃色的泥沙，如同一頭出籠的狂暴水獸，咆哮著倒灌入乾塢深處。不過眨眼之間，十米深的船塢底部已經化作一片翻騰的泥淖汪洋，水位正以每分鐘半米的可怕速度垂直飆升！\n\n「操！他不是要炸死咱們！」老周衝到門口，一把抓住門把手死命向外推，然而原本半掩的厚重鐵門已被外部落下的純鋼機械鎖舌死死卡死，「那王八蛋是要用三十年前淹死林清源博士的方式，把咱們三個活活溺死在這個乾塢的大鐵桶裡！」\n\n「門外是雙向重力落鎖，依靠水位浮標觸發，用手槍子彈無法擊穿四十五毫米的淬火合金鎖芯。」裴以安的聲音依舊冷靜得近乎殘酷，但他垂在身側的雙手已迅速扣緊了風衣袖口，「調度室距離乾塢底面只有四米，按照目前的江水倒灌流速，七分鐘內水面就會沒頂。」\n\n「別算了！快想辦法開門啊！」陸思遠癱軟在水流滲入的地板上，抱著大提琴盒子發出絕望的尖叫，「我不想死在水裡……我不想跟我父親一樣死在這條江裡！」\n\n「閉嘴！哭能把鎖哭開嗎？！」老周怒吼著揚起配槍，對準窗戶上的防爆夾膠玻璃接連扣動扳機。伴隨著刺耳的槍鳴，厚實的玻璃上只炸開了兩朵蛛網狀的白痕，在暴風雨中巍然不動。\n\n裴以安沒有去看窗戶，他的目光如手術刀般精準落在那座操作台上。\n\n在瘋狂擺動的節拍器正下方，赫然露出了一個由純紫銅鑄造的微型備用解鎖孔。鎖眼邊緣同樣雕刻著一條銜尾蛇，蛇口微張，正對著中央深邃的垂直插槽。\n\n「備用鎖孔。」裴以安迅速拔出那枚從林懷遠胃袋裡取出的黃銅鑰匙，然而當他將鑰匙探入鎖孔時，鑰匙卻在推進到三分之二處硬生生卡住了，「不對……齒痕深度相符，但鎖芯內部有一枚彈性反推阻尼。」\n\n「小裴！水已經漫過調度室的地板了！」老周看著冰冷渾濁的江水順著門縫如瀑布般湧入，淹沒了他們的腳踝，甚至漫到了那些懸空的鋼絲琴弦下方。\n\n裴以安取下眼鏡，從胸前口袋抽出那支純銀解剖鑷，緩緩探入鎖孔內壁。\n\n冰冷的手電光聚攏在鎖眼深處，只見純紫銅的鎖芯內壁上，並非普通的金屬彈子，而是整齊排列著四枚微型金屬音叉。音叉表面薄如蟬翼，正隨著室內節拍器的震盪發出極其微弱的共振嗡鳴。\n\n而在音叉後方的黃銅襯套上，用極細的鋼針刻著一行清晰的德文短句：\n\n**「唯有純正的八度共振，方能撫平冤魂的震顫。」**\n\n「這不是機械鎖，這是一座聲學諧振鎖！」裴以安猛然回頭，冰冷的目光直直刺向跪在地上的陸思遠，「這把鎖需要精確的聲波頻率觸發！陸思遠，拿出你的大提琴！」\n\n「什……什麼？拉琴？！」陸思遠渾身篩糠般發抖。\n\n「鎖芯裡的音叉規格是標準國際音高四百四十赫茲的倍頻。」裴以安一把扯開琴盒的卡扣，將那把通體泛著暗金色光澤的名貴古典大提琴硬生生塞進陸思遠懷裡，「用你的弓，拉C弦的大提琴泛音，精確維持在六十五點四赫茲！誤差不能超過零點五赫茲！」\n\n「我……我的手在抖……我拉不準……」陸思遠看著已經漫過小腿的刺骨江水，牙齒劇烈打顫。\n\n「陸思遠，聽著！」老周大步跨上前去，一把揪住年輕人的衣領，雙眼布滿血絲，聲音沙啞得宛如雷霆，「你不是濱江愛樂樂團的首席嗎？！三十年前你父親和陸崇山為了這把破琴奪走了別人的命！今天你要是拉不響這把琴，不僅對不起你手裡的弓，更對不起三十年前死在這座船廠裡的林清源！給我拉！」\n\n老周那充滿市井粗糲感與老刑警悍勇之氣的怒吼，如同一記重錘，狠狠砸在陸思遠的靈魂深處。\n\n年輕的大提琴家瞳孔劇烈收縮，淚水從他臉上滑落。在冰冷江水漫過膝蓋的瞬間，他那雙顫抖得不成樣子的雙手，在握緊琴弓與琴頸的剎那，竟奇蹟般地靜止了下來。\n\n那是刻進骨髓與肌肉記憶裡的十二萬個小時的苦練。\n\n陸思遠深吸了一口混雜著鐵鏽與江水的空氣，眼眸微闔，右臂在空中劃出一道決絕而優雅的弧度。\n\n「嗚——」\n\n深沉、渾厚、宛如受傷巨鯨哀鳴般的大提琴C弦泛音，在逼仄冰冷的調度室內轟然炸響！\n\n琴聲純粹得沒有一絲雜質，帶著穿透皮肉、直抵靈魂的悲愴。琴弦的振動波在空氣中擴散，精準地撞擊在純紫銅鎖孔內的微型音叉上！\n\n「錚——錚——錚——」\n\n四枚音叉在精確的頻率共振下劇烈震顫，帶動鎖芯內部的液壓阻尼瞬間卸壓！\n\n「就是現在！」裴以安眼神凌厲如電，握住黃銅鑰匙的手腕驟然發力，順時針狠狠扭動了整整一百八十度！\n\n「咔嚓——轟！」\n\n卡死在門框深處的鋼製鎖舌應聲彈開，厚重的鐵門在內外巨大的水壓差下轟然被撞開！\n\n「抓緊我！」老周怒吼著一把撈起陸思遠和大提琴盒，裴以安單手撐住門框，三人順著狂暴的江水激流，在千鈞一髮之際借著浮力衝出了懸空調度室，順著乾塢邊緣殘留的維修扶手，拼盡全力攀上了未被淹沒的高台！\n\n當三人渾身濕透、狼狽不堪地癱倒在冰冷的乾塢頂部水泥地面上時，腳下的二號乾塢已經徹底被奔騰的長江水吞沒，化作了一座深不見底的墨黑色深淵。\n\n破曉時分，十一月的江霧漸漸被天邊泛起的一抹魚肚白撕裂。\n\n遠處的老城碼頭方向，警笛聲呼嘯著由遠及近，刺目的紅藍警燈刺破了江邊的荒涼廢墟。\n\n裴以安半跪在泥濘中，呼吸微喘。他慢慢展開自己的右手掌心——在剛才解鎖彈開的瞬間，一枚藏在鎖芯最深處的微型純銀圓筒，被他順勢扣了出來。\n\n擰開銀筒，裡面倒出了一張被火漆蠟封、僅有兩指寬的古老羊皮紙條。\n\n老周拖著灌滿泥水的褲管湊了過來，手裡依舊死死攥著那隻印著大紅喜字的鐵皮保溫桶，氣喘吁吁地抹了一把臉上的水漬：「小裴……那老狐狸在鎖眼裡……留了什麼？」\n\n裴以安用戴著殘破乳膠手套的手指揭開火漆，展開了那張字條。\n\n晨曦微弱的冷光映照在字條上，上面是用優雅的哥德體法文與一行行楷中文寫就的親筆字跡：\n\n**「第一卷·序曲終了。黃銅鑰匙已經打開了被封存的三十年罪惡。然而，世間所有以謊言編織的榮耀，終將被刻骨的真相肢解。裴以安法醫，當第二場雨夜交響曲在濱江市現代藝術館奏響時，青銅的肋骨將向你敬禮。——擺渡人敬上」**\n\n老周死死盯著那張字條，長長地吐出了一口夾雜著泥腥味的白氣，嘴角泛起一絲老刑警冷酷而譏誚的笑意：「媽的……第二卷，這孫子還真打算給咱們來個連環套。」\n\n裴以安面無表情地站起身，迎著初升的冰冷江風，將羊皮紙條折好放入證物袋。\n\n他從口袋裡掏出一盒被雨水泡軟的鐵盒，取出一顆未沾水的薄荷糖放入口中，目光深邃地望向長江對岸那些隱沒在晨霧中的摩天高樓：\n\n「老周，叫蘇棠回實驗室準備吧。第一位死者的信我們已經讀完了。」\n\n裴以安推了一下沾滿雨滴的眼鏡架，薄唇微抿：\n\n「現在，該輪到我們去藝術館，聽聽青銅骨骼想對我們說什麼了。」","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 6: The Warning Inside the Keyhole\n\nNo sooner had the chilling chuckle faded from the transceiver than the deep machinery inside the suspended dispatch cabin's iron walls erupted with an ear-splitting screech of grinding gears.\n\n*Rumble—*\n\nThe entire suspended sheet-metal shack convulsed violently. The mechanical clockwork metronome—which had been ticking once every two seconds—suddenly surged into a frenzied blur, its needle sweeping across the calibrated dial and spitting out frantic, venomous *tick-tick-tick-ticks* like a striking serpent!\n\n\"Old Zhou! Beneath your feet!\" Pei Yi'an barked sharply.\n\nInside the corrugated sheet-metal partitions surrounding the cabin, neither lethal gas nor fire erupted; instead, the savage roar of rushing water tearing through sluice valves reverberated from the deep. Gazing through the floorboards, the two massive floodgates at the basin of Dry Dock Number Two—rusted shut and abandoned for decades—had been pried open a three-foot breach by concealed hydraulic rams!\n\nSwirling currents of the mighty Binjiang river—laden with biting river winds and yellowish-black silt—roared into the depths of the dry dock like a rampaging beast unchained from its cage. In the span of a single breath, the bottom of the ten-meter-deep dock was converted into a churning mud-swept sea, the waterline rocketing upward at an alarming half-meter per minute!\n\n\"Damn it! He's not trying to blow us up!\" Old Zhou lunged toward the doorway, violently throwing his weight against the iron door handle, yet the heavy steel leaf was hopelessly jammed by external deadbolts dropped into place. \"That bastard wants to drown the three of us alive in this dry-dock iron bucket—the exact same way he drowned Dr. Lin Qingyuan thirty years ago!\"\n\n\"The exterior is locked by bidirectional gravity deadbolts triggered by water-level floats; pistol rounds cannot breach forty-five-millimeter quenched alloy lock cylinders.\" Pei Yi'an's voice remained calm to the point of brutality, but his hands swiftly buttoned his cuffs at his sides. \"The dispatch cabin is only four meters above the dock floor; at the current flood rate, water will submerge this room completely within seven minutes.\"\n\n\"Stop calculating! Find a way to open the door!\" Collapsed on the flooding floorboards, Lu Siyuan clutched his cello case, unleashing a shriek of raw despair. \"I don't want to drown... I don't want to die in this river like my father!\"\n\n\"Shut up! Can your sobbing pick the lock?!\" Old Zhou snarled as he leveled his sidearm, firing two consecutive rounds into the explosion-proof laminated glass of the window. Amid the deafening muzzle blasts, only two spiderweb fractures blossomed across the dense glass, remaining utterly unyielding against the storm.\n\nPei Yi'an didn't glance at the window; his eyes settled upon the iron console with the precision of a surgical scalpel.\n\nDirectly beneath the wildly swinging metronome, a miniature emergency bypass cylinder forged of pure red copper was revealed. The rim of the keyhole was likewise engraved with an ouroboros, its mouth slightly parted, framing the deep vertical aperture in its center.\n\n\"An auxiliary bypass.\" Pei Yi'an swiftly produced the brass key recovered from Lin Huaiyuan's stomach, yet when he slid the key into the slot, it jammed rigidly at two-thirds depth. \"Incorrect... the bitting depth matches, but an elastic counter-thrust damper resists from within.\"\n\n\"Little Pei! The water is already washing across the cabin deck!\" Old Zhou watched as turbid, icy river water cascaded through the door seams like miniature waterfalls, submerging their ankles and rising toward the suspended cello strings.\n\nRemoving his spectacles, Pei Yi'an drew his solid-silver dissecting forceps from his breast pocket and gently guided the tips along the inner cylinder wall.\n\nThe cold beam of the flashlight pooled into the keyhole. Lining the interior cylinder was no ordinary pin-tumbler assembly; instead, four miniature acoustic tuning forks stood aligned with razor precision. Delicate as cicada wings, their tines hummed with a faint sympathetic vibration in response to the frantic metronome.\n\nAnd on the brass bushing behind the tuning forks, an ultra-fine steel stylus had incised a clear German aphorism:\n\n**\"Only pure octaval resonance can soothe the shudder of an aggrieved ghost.\"**\n\n\"This is no mechanical lock; this is an acoustic resonance lock!\" Pei Yi'an spun around, his piercing gaze spearing straight toward the kneeling Lu Siyuan. \"This cylinder requires an exact acoustic frequency to disarm! Lu Siyuan, take out your cello!\"\n\n\"Wh... what? Play my cello?!\" Lu Siyuan shook violently like a sifter.\n\n\"The tuning forks are calibrated to octave harmonics of international pitch standard 440 Hz.\" Pei Yi'an ripped open the latches of the hardcase, thrusting the antique, dark-gold concert cello straight into Lu Siyuan's arms. \"Use your bow. Sound the cello flageolet overtone on the C-string, holding it precisely at 65.4 Hertz! Tolerance cannot exceed 0.5 Hertz!\"\n\n\"My... my hands are shaking... I can't play in tune...\" Looking down at the freezing river water lapping past his shins, Lu Siyuan's teeth rattled uncontrollably.\n\n\"Lu Siyuan, listen to me!\" Striding forward through the surging water, Old Zhou grabbed the young musician by the lapels, his bloodshot eyes blazing, his voice crashing like thunder: \"Aren't you the concertmaster of the Binjiang Philharmonic?! Thirty years ago, your father and Lu Chongshan took another man's life for this godforsaken instrument! If you can't make this cello sing tonight, you not only fail the bow in your hands, you fail Lin Qingyuan who died in this shipyard thirty years ago! Now play!\"\n\nOld Zhou's roar—steeped in raw street grit and the fierce, unyielding courage of a veteran detective—struck like a sledgehammer into the depths of Lu Siyuan's soul.\n\nThe young cellist's pupils contracted violently as tears streamed down his cheeks. As the frigid river water lapped past his knees, those hands that had been trembling uncontrollably suddenly stilled into absolute, miraculous stillness the instant his fingers wrapped around the bow and fingerboard.\n\nIt was twelve thousand hours of relentless discipline etched into his bone marrow and muscle memory.\n\nTaking a deep breath of air dense with rust and river silt, Lu Siyuan lowered his eyelids, his right arm sweeping through the air with resolute, tragic grace.\n\n*Wooo—*\n\nA deep, cavernous, weeping flageolet harmonic on the C-string—sounding like the mournful cry of a wounded leviathan—detonated inside the claustrophobic sheet-metal cabin!\n\nThe tone was pure beyond measure, vibrating through bone and soul with bottomless sorrow. The acoustic waves expanded through the damp air, striking with mathematical precision against the micro-tuning forks inside the copper keyhole!\n\n*Hum—hum—hum—*\n\nThe four tuning forks shuddered violently in sympathetic resonance, triggering the internal hydraulic dampener to bleed off its pressure in an instant!\n\n\"Now!\" Pei Yi'an's eyes flashed with electric intensity. Wrenching the brass key with his full grip, he turned it clockwise a full one hundred and eighty degrees!\n\n*Clack—BOOM!*\n\nThe steel deadbolt jammed inside the doorframe disengaged, and the massive iron door blew outward under the colossal hydraulic pressure differential between inside and out!\n\n\"Hold on to me!\" Old Zhou roared, scooping up Lu Siyuan and the cello case with one arm. Gracing the doorframe with one hand, Pei Yi'an rode the surging current with them as the buoyant force expelled all three through the threshold in the nick of time, clawing their way along the dock's retaining railings until they collapsed onto the unsubmerged high concrete platform!\n\nWhen the three lay sprawled, soaked and gasping across the freezing concrete edge of the dock, Dry Dock Number Two beneath them had been thoroughly swallowed by the raging waters of the Binjiang, transformed into an abyss of ink-black fury.\n\nAt daybreak, the November river mist began tearing apart under the pale fish-belly grey horizon.\n\nFrom the direction of the old municipal wharves, sirens wailed as they approached, their dazzling crimson and azure flashers cutting through the desolate wreckage of the shipyard.\n\nHalf-kneeling in the mud, Pei Yi'an caught his breath. He slowly uncurled his right palm—during the final instant when the lock popped open, his fingertips had deftly slipped out a miniature solid-silver capsule concealed deep within the cylinder core.\n\nTwisting open the silver capsule, a rolled strip of ancient parchment sealed in red sealing wax—barely two fingers wide—tumbled out into his palm.\n\nDragging waterlogged trouser cuffs through the mire, Old Zhou shuffled over, still clutching his tin thermos stamped with the red double-happiness character, panting as he wiped muddy spray from his face: \"Little Pei... what did that old fox... leave in the keyhole?\"\n\nPeeling away the wax seal with his torn latex glove, Pei Yi'an unfurled the parchment strip.\n\nThe faint, cold light of dawn glinted across the parchment, revealing handwritten lines executed in elegant Gothic French alongside neat rows of Chinese brushwork:\n\n**\"Volume One · The Overture Concludes. The brass key has unsealed thirty years of buried sin. Yet, all honors woven of falsehood shall inevitably be dismembered by the bone-deep truth. Dr. Pei Yi'an, when the second movement of the rainy night symphony sounds at the Binjiang Museum of Modern Art, the bronze ribs shall salute you. —Respectfully, The Ferryman\"**\n\nStaring fixedly at the parchment, Old Zhou exhaled a long plume of white vapor tinged with the scent of river mud, a cold, sardonic grin curling at the edges of the veteran detective's lips: \"Damn it... Volume Two. That grandson really intends to put us through a meat grinder.\"\n\nExpressionless, Pei Yi'an rose to his feet, facing the biting morning breeze coming off the river, carefully folding the parchment into a fresh evidence pouch.\n\nFishing a rain-softened tin box from his pocket, he slipped an unblemished peppermint lozenge into his mouth, his gaze piercing through the morning fog toward the skyscrapers across the river:\n\n\"Old Zhou, notify Su Tang to prepare the laboratory. We have finished reading the first corpse's letter.\"\n\nPei Yi'an nudged his raindrops-spattered glasses frame, his thin lips setting into a resolute line:\n\n\"Now, it's our turn to visit the art museum, and hear what the bronze bones have to say to us.\""}];
